Indian_Farming_November_2025.pdf_024,other_docs,Indian_Farming_November_2025.pdf,24,"It is believed that the principles and practices of watershed hydrology will resolve the national land and water degradation problems. The textbook is divided into 13 Chapters. Beginning with general introduction to hydrology, it covers the chapter-wise global and Indian water balance, precipitation measurement and analysis procedures. TECHNICAL ASPECTS Pages: v + 478; Price: ` 1000.00, US$ 90.00; Postage: `50 ISBN No. : 978-81-7164-203-8 For obtaining copies, please contact: SCAN QR Code to Business Unit Purchase Online ICAR-Directorate of Knowledge Management in Agriculture Krishi Anusandhan Bhawan – I, Pusa, New Delhi 110012 Tel: 011-25843657; email: businessuniticar@gmail.com website: www.icar.org.in Indian Farming 19 November 2025 Indian Farming 75 (11): 20-22; November 2025 Remote sensing applications in monitoring and management of soil and water pollution Krishan Kanahiya*, Parul Sundha and D. S. Bundela ICAR-Central Soil Salinity Research Institute, Karnal, Haryana 132 001 Pollution of soil and water is major problem all around the world that effects the condition of ecosystem, agricultural productivity and well-being of human lifestyles. Traditionally, tracking and managing these problems require a lotof fieldwork, which can be laborious, time consuming and has limited both spatial and geographical coverage. A useful alternative is remote sensing, offers a promising alternative by making it possible to gather data from multiple sensors on a large scale and frequently. This article addresses the newest developments, methods and data types in the field of remote sensing, which investigates how remote sensing can be used to track and control soil and water pollution. Keywords: Ecosystem, Remote sensing, Soil and water pollution, Tracking INDIA has achieved tremendous progress in remote Principles of remote sensing in pollution monitoring sensing technology, with numerous centres and Remote sensing (RS) is a technique that collects data organization devoted towards the applications, research regarding the Earth's surface from afar, utilizing sensors and policy creation in this area. The supreme institute affixed to satellites, airplanes and drones. It is based on for space organization for space research is Indian detection and analysing electromagnetic energy that is Space Research Organisation (ISRO). It runs a huge absorbed or released by objects. Specific spectral patterns network of earth observation satellite, which include linked with pollutants or environmental changes may CartoSat, ResourseSat and RISAT series, offer useful be helpful in the detection and quantification of soil and information for tracking the soil and water pollution. Its water contamination levels. Remote sensing collects subsidiary organisations like National remote sensing hyperspectral, thermal and multi-spectral data that may centre (NRSC), Hyderabad and Indian Institution of Remote Sensing (IIRS), Dehradun play a crucial role be examined and processed for recognizing pollution for development of satellites and carrying out capacity- anomalies. building initiatives. The Northern Space Application centre (NESAC) covers the specific requirements of Types of remote sensing data for pollution monitoring the northeast region, whereas the Ahmedabad based Different data types are used in remote sensing space application centre (SAC) emphasized on sensor applications for pollution monitoring, which have development. Remote sensing technology also used specific advantages to identify soil and water in research institute and agricultural universities like contaminations.",508,en,2025.0
