r-holding capacity. Adoption of efficient irrigation methods, such as drip or alternate furrow irrigation, minimizes salt accumulation near the root zone. Utilization of plant growth-promoting rhizobacteria (PGPR) and arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi (AMF) enhances nutrient uptake, root growth, and stress tolerance under saline conditions.Recent advancements in nanotechnology have introduced the application of nano- encapsulated nutrients and engineered nanoparticles, which improve nutrient absorption, physiological efficiency, and Strategies to develop salt tolerance mustard variety plant growth under saline environments. Indian Farming 25 November 2025 SUMMARY of the genetic basis of salinity tolerance but also facilitate Indian mustard is a moderately resilient crop that the development of molecular markers and gene targets requires relatively less irrigation and can tolerate for breeding programmes focused on improving salinity moderate levels of soil salinity, making it a promising resilience in mustard. crop for cultivation in salt-affected areas. However, to To achieve this, it is crucial to integrate conventional fully harness its potential, extensive reservoir of mustard breeding approaches with modern biotechnological germplasm must be systematically explored to identify tools and sustainable agronomic practices. Advanced genotypes with superior resilience and adaptability to technologies such as genome editing, in combination saline soils, without compromising seed yield or oil with omics-based approaches including genomics, quality. There are relatively few reports available on the transcriptomics, proteomics, and metabolomics hold identification of novel genes and quantitative trait loci immense potential to unravel the complex mechanisms underlying salinity tolerance. The integration of these (QTLs) associated with salinity tolerance in mustard.",504,en,2025.0
