e to stresses such as salinity and sodicity. For instance, integrating salt-tolerant crops like quinoa, barley, or specific rice and wheat varieties alongside traditional crops can enhance soil management in saline or sodic areas. 2. Efficient water management: Efficient water management techniques in farming focus on optimizing water use, minimizing wastage, and preventing waterlogging that worsens soil salinity and sodicity. Methods such as drip irrigation deliver water directly to plant roots, reducing evaporation and salt buildup, while precision farming applies water only where and when needed to conserve resources. Proper water management helps mitigate salinity/sodicity effects, enhances crop productivity, and lowers agriculture’s environmental impact. Techniques like rainwater harvesting and recycling • When the farmer intends to maximize profits from supplement irrigation, reducing reliance on the current landholding. groundwater in saline and sodic regions. • When the farmer is motivated to minimize 3. Soil health improvement: Soil health improvement environmental pollution. aims to enhance fertility, structure, and biological Table 1. Enterprises linked in different agro-ecosystem activity, which are vital for sustainable crop production. Techniques like composting, green Dry Agro- Farm Dairy Poultry Goat/sheep manuring, and vermiculture increase soil organic land forestry pond matter, boosting nutrient and water retention. Healthy soils are more resilient to salinity and Garden Bee Dairy Poultry Mushroom Piggery Sericulture land Keeping sodicity stresses and support diverse microbial communities that aid nutrient cycling and plant Wet health.",493,en,2025.0
