LeafblightSouvenirArticle.pdf.pdf_000,other_docs,LeafblightSouvenirArticle.pdf.pdf,0,"63 व␀ अिखल भारतीय गेहूं एवं जौ अनुसंधानकता␀ गो␀ठी 63rd All India Wheat & Barley Research Worker's Meet flrEcj 11&13] 2024 |September 11-13, 2024 ␀मा␀रका Souvenir आचाय␀ नर␀␀ देव क␀िष एवं ␀ौ␀ोिगकी िव␀विव␀ालय, अयो␀या (उ␀र ␀देश) Acharya Narendra Deva University of Agriculture & Technology, Ayodhya (Uttar Pradesh) & भा.क␀.अनु.प.-भारतीय गेहूं एवं जौ अनुसंधान सं␀थान, करनाल (ह␀रयाणा) ICAR-Indian Institute of Wheat & Barley Research, Karnal (Haryana) CONTENTS S.N. Particulars Page No. Invited Lectures 1. ANDUA&T: profile, achievements and strategic vision 01 Bijendra Singh 2. History, present status and prospects of wheat in Uttar Pradesh 07 Vinod Kumar Singh, Anupam Tripathi, Deepak Prajapati, Piyusha Singh and Priyanka Jaiswal 3. Barley improvement with special reference to Uttar Pradesh 11 Priyanka Jaiswal, Vinod Kumar Singh and Piyusha Singh 4. CIMMYT's vision for food security in developing countries through 16 new frontiers in wheat improvement Velu Govindan, Pradeep Bhati, Pawan K. Singh, Arun K. Joshi and Kevin Pixley 5. Agri-resources optimization through natural farming 25 Anil Kumar Khippal, Shambhunath Ghosh, SC Gill, RS Chhokar, Neeraj Kumar, OP Ahlawat, PL Kashyap, Kamini Kumari, Rinki, Mamrutha HM, Charu Lata, Koushal Kishore Bijarnia, Satyavir Singh and SC Tripathi 6. Recent agronomic technologies for improving wheat productivity and profitability 30 Subhash Chander Gill, RS Chhokar, Neeraj Kumar, Anil Kumar Khippal, SC Tripathi, Shiv Ram Samota, Nitesh Kumar and Vikramjeet Singh 7. Recent development in improving seed replacement rate in wheat and barley 35 AK Sharma, UR Kamble, Sripathy KV, BS Tyagi and Ratan Tiwari 8. Strategies for promotion of hull-less barley as nutri-cereal 43 Omvir Singh, Lokendra Kumar, Jogendra Singh, SK Bishnoi, Chuni Lal, OP Gupta, Rekha Malik and R Tiwari 9. Enhancing barley productivity in salt affected agro-ecosystems in India 47 Arvind Kumar, Neeraj Kulshrestha, Om Vir Singh and Santosh Kumar Bishnoi 10. Enhancing wheat productivity in salinity-alkalinity affected areas 53 Neeraj Kulshreshtha and Arvind Kumar 11. Novel techniques targeting genetic gains in wheat 58 Hanif Khan, Sonia Sheoran, Mamrutha HM and Ratan Tiwari 12. Effective utilization of national and international nurseries in 63 wheat improvement programme Arun Gupta, BS Tyagi, Charan Singh, RK Bairwa, OP Ahlawat and Ratan Tiwari 13. Wheat quality parameters and their relevance 67 Om Prakash Gupta, Sunil Kumar, Vanita Pandey, Anuj Kumar, Sewa Ram and Ratan Tiwari 14. Wheat germplasm and stocks developed for climate resilience, 71 resistance to biotic stresses and superior quality BS Tyagi, Vikas Gupta, Arun Gupta, Amit K Sharma, Charan Singh, Satish Kumar, CN Mishra, UR Kamble, Gyanendra Singh and Ratan Tiwari 15. Leaf blight of wheat and barley: detection, diagnosis and management 78 Ravindra Kumar, Pradeep Sharma, PL Kashyap, Sudhir Navathe, SS Vaish, PS Shekhawat, Ishwar Singh, Shubham Raj, Aishwarya Singh Rathore and Ratan Tiwari 63RD ALL INDIA WHEAT AND BARLEY RESEARCH WORKER’S MEET, ANDUAT, KUMARGANJ, AYODHYA, SEPT. 11-13, 2024 Leaf blight of wheat and barley: detection, diagnosis and management Ravindra Kumar1, Pradeep Sharma1, PL Kashyap1, Sudhir Navathe2, S.S. Vaish3, P.S. Shekhawat4, Ishwar Singh1, Shubham Raj1, Aishwarya Singh Rathore1&5 and Ratan Tiwari1 (Hordeum spp.)",496,en,2024.0
