Advisory for management of Cucumber Mosaic Virus (CMV) on Banana Crop.pdf_002,ppqs_advisories,Advisory for management of Cucumber Mosaic Virus (CMV) on Banana Crop.pdf,2,"Farmers must be educated to identify, conserve and augment lhe natural enemies (parasitoides/predators like Spiderr, Ludy Bird beetle, gfeen lacewing' predatory mites' Bracon hebetor, Trichogram;; tp:and i{over fly) available fnlhe banana fields' 6. Set up yellow water par/sticky ffis for monitoring aphid @ 4-5 traps/acre at the height of mid canopy' -)- 7. Grow Marigold, Sunflower, Mustard, Cowpea to attract the predators viz',-coccinelids such as scymnus, chiromenes sexmaculitus, and lacewings such as Chrysoperla zastrowi sillemi, predatory mantids, ladybird beetles and parasitic wasps' g. Remove infected ptants frtm fields and destroy them by buming or digging deep inside soil. 9. The banana fields should be kept free from weeds' 10. Infected suckers should not be used for planting' 11. Weeds in the nearby areas should be removed as the virus survives in them in off season. 12. P D e e st t i a ci i d le es d s i h n o fo u r ld m b a e ti o u n sed a is s pe a r l v a a be il l a c b la le im o a n pp ro d v ir e e d c t b o y ra t t h e e 's co a m t m itt l e in e k . fi on ://ooqs.sov.inlsi 01.06.2023.pdf A list of recommended pesticides and for aphids in banana is attached at Annexure-I. Further the fotlowing strategies should be adopted for spreading awareness among farmers o Mobilization of extension functionaries at grass route level for regular monitoring of CI\{V status and ensure CMV free planting material' o Regular meetings of State Pest Surveillance and advisory unit and District Pest Surveillance and Advisory Unit may be conducted o Awareness among farming community through newspapers, printing and electronic media, Kisan Gosthi,leaflet and pamphlets' o The concerned officials at the district/ divisiorV block level may be advised to take the suitable plant protection measures immediately The detailed information on pest incidence may also be sent to the directorate through email to ppa@nic.in or appa.ipm-dppqs@gov.in urgently to apprise the same to Department of Agtt. ""tt""* & FamA;' Welfare, MoA&FW, Government of India' Yours faithfully (Dr.J.P.Singh) Plant Protection Adviser Copy for information: 1. pps to Joint Secretary(PP), DA& FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 2. The Directors of Agriculture/tlorticulture of other banana growing states with the request to keep close watch on pest build up & take appropriate measures as indicated above 3. PPS to PPA for information 4. officer In-charges, all cIPMCs of banana growing states with directions to conduct regular survey in the area to ensure and necessary follow-up with the state authorities. Annexure-f crBRC Approved pesticides for the contror of Aphids in Banana Dilution in Water Oxydemeton-metM-",463,en,2023.0
Advisory for management of Rice leaf folder (Cnaphalocrocis medinalis) on Rice crop.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory for management of Rice leaf folder (Cnaphalocrocis medinalis) on Rice crop.pdf,0,"@ ffi ,ffi {c'q<rrrF'w:dtgft *r Phone: 0129-2413985 E-mail:-ppa@nic.in "" TR \t{ frq|. ;f 6-€{rur {'Trcq / Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare TR \t4 fiffiT s""ilTot Rrrr{r / Department of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare ffr€qft {i{qTut, ffiq qq Tir{ R?qrmq / Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine & Storage 5 g<4, m-t-<r+r< ({ftTrurD - t2I 001/ NH-IV, Faridabad (Haryana) - I 2 1 00 I Dated: 25.09.2023 To The Director of Horticulture Govt. of Odisha, Punjab and Haryana Sub: Advisory for management of Rice leaf folder (Cnaphalocrocis medinalis) on rice crop -reg. Sir, It is to bring to your notice that incidence of Rice leaf fold er (Cnaphalocrocis medinalis) on rice crop is reported in the,Odisha, Punjab and Haryana region. The pest was reported in Faridkot districts of Punjab, Cuttak and Dhrnkanal districts of Odisha and Sonipat district of Haryana at moderate intensity (Area affected2900 ha in Punjab). Keeping in view the current crop stage and prevailing weather condition, Integrated Pest Management techniques should be adopted. IPM Package of practices of Rice is availablb at DPPQ&S website in the link https://ppqs.gov.inlipm-packages. Important IPM for management of Rice Leaf Folder are listed below 1. Low usage of nitrogenous fertilizers decreases lgftf damage. Highly fertilized plots seem to attract females for oviposition. Theref-ot€, it is advisable to avoid over- fertilization. 2. Egg predators (crickets) inhabit surrounding grass habitats and move to the field at night for predation. Maintenance of non-rice habitats. 3. Higher damages will occur in shaded areas. Therefore, remove the causes of shading within the fielC. 4. Removal and destruction of diseased/pest infested plant parts. 5. Use of coir rope in rice crop for dislodging leaf folder larvae etc. on to kerosinized water (1 L of kerosene mixed on 25kg soil and broadcast in tha). 6. Remove grassy weeds from fields and borders. 7. Flood and plough field after harvesting if possible. 8. Rotate rice with a diffsrent crop, or have a fallow period. 9. Avoid ratooning 10. Encor:lrage predators such as spider, parasitic wasps, predatory beetles, frogs and dragon fly. 11. Encourage biological control agents like Trichogramma japonicum and T chilonis may be released @ I lal<h/ha on appearance of egg masses / moth of leaf folder in the field, Egg Parasitoid Copidosomopsis nacoleiae, Larval Parasitoid Stenobracon nicevillei, Larval and Pupal Parasitoid Brachymeria lasus, B. excarinata etc. tl -2- 12. Encourage the use of biopesticides/ botanicals to manage the pest so as to avoid it to reach to ETL. 13. pesticides should be used on p c e e t a th ile e a p e i s n t f r o ea ; c a he i; s r E i T r L u u a u n i d la as b l p ; e o r n l a d b ir e e l c c to la r i a m te a 's p p w r e o b ve s d ite b a y t the registration committee.",501,en,2023.0
