Advisory for management of Rice Stem Borer (Scirpophaga incertulas on rice crop.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory for management of Rice Stem Borer (Scirpophaga incertulas on rice crop.pdf,0,"ffi ffi Phone: 0129-2413985 E-mail:-ppa@nic.in "" TR \-{ tqffitq 6""rtrur {Trflq / Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare FR \rd ftsr{ +.-e{nur fttrrr / Department of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare T{€qft {i(qpt, ffiE q{ {fr{ Ftqrrcq / Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine & Storage qq qq.4, sftqTq-K teRqrun - nl001/ NH-IV, Faridabad (Haryana) - 121 001 Dated: 25.09.2023 To The Director of Horticulture Govt. of Maharashtra, Punjab and Haryana Sub: Advisory for management of Rice Stem Borer (Scirpophaga incertulud on rice crop -reg. Sir, . . It is to bring to your notice that incidence of Rice Stem Borer (Scirpophaga incertulad on rice crop is reponed in the Maharashtra, Punjab and Haryana states. The pest was reported in Gadchiioli districts of Maharashtra above ETL (Area affected 23599.24 ha) and Amritsar district and SBS Nagar of Punjab at moderate level (Area affected 550 ha and 77 ha, respectively) and Sonipat, Jind and Kaithal districts of Haryanaattrace to low level. Keeping in view the current crop stage and prevailing weather condition, Integrated Pest Management techniques should be adopted. IPM Package of practices of Rice is available at DPPQ&S website in the link https://ppqs.gov.inlipm-packages. Impgrtant IPM for management of Rice Stem Borer are listed below 1. Monitoring of field at weekly intervals/regularly 2. Handpick and destroY egg masses 3. Removal and destruction of diseased/pest infeste@Iant parts. 4. Field should be necessarily scouted during the vulnerable crop growth stages for early detection of dead hearts and white ear. 5. Raise level of inigation water periodically to submerge the eggs deposited on the lower parts of the Plant. 6. Installation of light trap @ llha and pheromone trap @ 10-12lha for monitoring/ controlling adults. . Apply nitrogen fertilizer in split following the recommended rate and time of 7 application. 8. Avoid high dose fettilizet. g. Five to six releases of the eggparasitoid Trichogramma iaponicum or T chilonit @ 1,00,000 adult parasites per hectare starting from 15 days after planting. 10. Encourage biological control agents: Tetrastichus schoenobii, Telenomus rowani, Amauromorpha accepta, Cotesia flavipes, Xanthopimpla flavolineota, Pardosa pseudoannulata (wolf spider) etc. 1 1. Recommended botanicals/ biopesticides should be used to manage the pest so as to avoid it to reach to ETL p -2- 12. Pesticides should be used once the pest is repbrted above ETL and as per label claim approved by the registration committee. Detailed information is available on directorate's website at link hltps://ppqs.gov.ir/sites/defaulVfiles/1 :--major-use-qfuiestigides-inpgctiqides-4s-ofr* 0'l.06,2Q23.pdf A list of recommended pesticides for rice stem borer is attached at Annexure-I. Further the following strategies should be adopted for spreading awareness itmong farmers o Mobilization of extension functionaries at grass route level for regular monitoring of pest status. i o Regular meetings of State Pest Surveillance and advisory unit and District Pest Suweillance and Advisory Unit may be conducted . Awareness among farming community through newspapers, printing and electronic media, Kisan Gosthi, leaflet and pamphlets.",478,en,2023.0
Advisory for management of Rice Stem Borer (Scirpophaga incertulas on rice crop.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Advisory for management of Rice Stem Borer (Scirpophaga incertulas on rice crop.pdf,1,"i o Regular meetings of State Pest Surveillance and advisory unit and District Pest Suweillance and Advisory Unit may be conducted . Awareness among farming community through newspapers, printing and electronic media, Kisan Gosthi, leaflet and pamphlets. o ThE concerned officials at the district/ divisior/ block levql may be advised to take the suitable plant protection measures immediately The detailed information on pest incidence may also be sent to the directorate through email to ppa@nic.in or appa.ipm-dppqs@gov.in urgently to apprise the same to Department of Agriculture & Farmers' Welf4re, MoA&FW, Government of India. Yours faithfullv P (Dr.J.P.Singh) Plant Protection Adviser Copy for information: 1 . PPS to Joint Secretary(PP), DA& FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 2. The Directors ofAgriculture/tlorticulture of other rice growing states with the requestto keep close watch on pest build up & take appropriate measures as indicated above 3. PPS to PPA for information 4. Officer In-charges, all CIPMCs of rice growing states with directions to conduct regular survey in the area to ensure and necessary follow-up with the state authorities.",176,en,2023.0
