Advisory for management of White Rust on Mustard crop.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory for management of White Rust on Mustard crop.pdf,0,"ffi ffi Phone: 0129-2413985 E-mai1:-ppa@nic.in F.No 3:6i2022-23lIPlWAdvisory sIT<f {IFffV Government of India FR qi Rqrt +-eqr""ur riTrdq / Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare FR qd frvr{ +-eqrur frqFr f Department of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare qtwR d<qur, {rr+E q* Tif{ R?crFc I Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine & Storage qil qs4, s'fr-ff{r{ (€RqrurT) - 12 I 001/ NH-IV, Faridabad (Haryana) - I 2 I 00 I Dated: 15.02.2024 fo The Director of Agriculture Govt. of Haryana sub: Advisory for management of white Rust on Mustard crop -reg. Sir, it is to bring to your notice that incidence of White Rust caused by Atbugo candida on Mustard crop is reported in Sirsa and Fatehabad districts of Haryana. In Fatehabad district, in 2112.5 acres out of 60925 acres of total area of mustard crop i.e., up to 25Yo damage was observed. The symptoms of disease appears as white to creamy yellow pustules on the lower surface of leaves. The pustules, later coalesce to form patches on the lower surface of leaves. Moist (more than7}%o relative humidity) coupled with warm weather and intermittent rains favours disease development. The fungus is likely to damage mustard crop, which has potential to bring down the average yield by 30-40% in late sowrr crops. It is at the initial stage and unlikely to cause major damage if farmers take timely measures. Keeping in view the current crop stage and prevailing weather condition, disease may spread further. Important IPM for management of White Rust are listed below 1. Removal and complete destruction of diseased infested plant parts by buming so that the further spread of diseases is reduced. 2. Clean cultivation helps to avoid disease incidence. 3. Get rid of the weeds in and around the field. 4. Fungicides should be used as per label claim approved by the registration committee. Detailed information is available on directorate's website at link httos:/ inlsites/defl ior use of 0L06.2023.odf A list of recommended fungicides for white rust of mustard is attached at Annexure-I. Further the following strategies should be adopted for spreading awareness among farmers o Mobilization of extension functionaries at grass route level for regular monitoring of white rust in mustard. o Regular meetings of State Pest Surveillance and advisory unit and District Pest Surveillance and Advisory Unit may be conducted to check further spread of mustard white rust. o Awareness among farming community through newspapers, printing and electronic media, Kisan Gosthi, leaflet and pamphiets for plant protection measures. o The concetned officials at the district/ division/ block level may be advised to take the suitable plant protection measures accordingly. -1- The detailed information on pest incidence may also be sent to the directorate through email to ppa@nic.in or appa.ipm-dppqs@,gov.in ulgently to apprise the same to Department of eF""tt*"" & Farmers' Welfare, MoA&FW, Govemment of India. Yours faithfirlly bND/ 4_V (Dr.J.P.Singh) Plant Protection Adviser . Copy for information: 1. PPS to Joint SecretaryGP), DA& FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 2.",493,en,2024.0
