Advisory on current status of Gall midge (Orseolia oryzae) infesting Paddy crop in Tamil Nadu State.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on current status of Gall midge (Orseolia oryzae) infesting Paddy crop in Tamil Nadu State.pdf,0,"?Fftslq/Tele: o I 29-24 1398s fr-ffi/Fux, 0129-2412125 ffi'WPL',$ E-mail: npa@nic.in F. No. 3-6i2019-20/IPM-AdvisorY s{[{d q{fiRiGovern m e n t of I n d ia T;R W m€f+ FF[tut qTftrqnuin istry of Ag ric u ltu re & Fa rm e rs Wel fa re q;fr{T€:6fREf qniftfUf+W@fuf ftqSqlp.Ourtment of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farmers Welfare T{€qfr {ip{uf, UtffrU qrti *ff6 frkff6qt Directorate Of Plant Protection, Quarantine And Storage qq.qq.-4, rn{iqrcnE, €furun / N.H.IV. FARIDABAD IHARYANA) Date: \5unuury ,2020 To The Director of Agriculture, Department of Agriculture Government of Tamil Nadu Chepauk, Chennai 600005 Tamil Nadu Sub:- Advisory on current status of Gall midge (Orseolia oryzae) infesting Paddy crop in Tamil Nadu State-reg. Sir. I have the honour to bring to your kind notice that incidence of Rice gall midge has been reported in paddy crop at low to moderate intensity in Pudukkottai, Thanjarnrr and Tiruvallur districts of Tamil Nadu State during the video conference held on 24""' December, 2019 atitishi Bhawan, New Delhi' Rice gall midge is a pest of paddy crop, causes a tubular gall at the base of tillers, causing elongation of leaf sheaths called onion leaf or silver shoot. The population density of the rice gall midge is favored mainly by cloudy or rainy weather. In view of the prevailing congenial weather conditions, the chance of incidence of rice gall midge is high and pest management interventions are imperative to check the possible population buildup. The following practices of IPM strategies may be followed for management of Gall midge infestation in PaddY croP: o Practice early ploughing immediately after harvest of the paddy crop. o Planting of early maturing resistant/ tolerant varieties may help to avoid high infestations. o Plow ratoon of the previous crop and remove all off-season plant hosts (grassy weeds and wild rice) from surrounding aleas can reduce gall midge incidence. o Conserve natural enemies: platygasterid, eupelmid, and pteromalid wasps (parasitize the larvae), phytoseiid mites (feed on eggs) and spiders (feed on adults). o Using only moderate amounts of nitrogen and potassium fertilizers and adopting split t' applications to reduce population growth rates. Avoiding staggered planting (complete trans-planting in an arca within 3 weeks) to reduce infestation. Draining out water from paddy fields for 5-7 days will drastically bring down Gall midge population. The Gall midge adults are found to be active between dusk time (6 to 10 PM) and hence light traps @ 1No. Per acre can be operated between 6 to 10 PM to attract Gall midge adults. In the event of severe infestation of Gall midge, application of any of the plant based products like l0% Neem leaf extract,5oh NSKE, 1olo Neem orl,0.3Yo Fish oil resin soap,3o/o Dasagavya and 3o/o Herbal plant extraction can be sprayed to bring down the pest population. o Collect and destroy infbsted crop debris. a Maintain field sanitation.",470,en,2020.0
Advisory on current status of Gall midge (Orseolia oryzae) infesting Paddy crop in Tamil Nadu State.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on current status of Gall midge (Orseolia oryzae) infesting Paddy crop in Tamil Nadu State.pdf,1,"o Collect and destroy infbsted crop debris. a Maintain field sanitation. a A strong and fool proof quality control system for fertilizers, bio-fertilizers, insecticides needs to be enforced' Regular training programme for the extension workers, pesticide dealers and farmers should be organized !y the SAUs/ICAR Institutes/CIPMCs/KVKs for up-gradation of their knowledge and skills regarding management of Gall midge' Insecticides must be used as per label claim approved by the Central Insecticide Board and Registration Committee (CIB&RC). Detailed information is available at However, list of http://ppqs.goiirVdivisions/cibrc/major-uses-of-pesticides. ii.o--.nded Insecticides for Rice Gall midge is attached (Annexure-I)' Farmers should be advised through extension functionaries to use only recommended doses of fertilizers and Insecticides as per approved label claims by CIB&RC. The IPM p^a ckage of practices for Rice needs to be promoted. The IPM package of foi Rice may be downloaded from web-link practices http ://ppqs. gov. irVsites/defaulti fi les/rice. pd1 In view of the congenial weather conditions, it is advised to undertake monitoring of Rice crop on regular basis. tf Gall midge incidence is reported by the farmers or by any other source, ,ur,r""y of t6. affected area may be conducted immediately and the concerned officials at district/divisiorVblock may be advised to take need based plant protection measures to avoid economic loss. The hot spots of Gall midge should be identified through suruey for regular monitoring. The detailed information may also be sent to the Directorate through e-mail appa.ipm-ipqs@eov.in urgently to apprise the same to Department of Agriculture, Cooperation and Farmers Welfare. Encl: As above tl PH{i*<"", (Raj