Advisory on current status of Thrips( Thrips tabaci) for Cotton growing areas of Gujarat.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on current status of Thrips( Thrips tabaci) for Cotton growing areas of Gujarat.pdf,0,"E-mail: ppa. @nic.in ffi tfistdrr eb : o 12924 1 3 9 8 s *qWFa*: 0129-2412125 qr +i.Aqo. 3-6/2018-l9,llPM-Advisory flRA T{6R/Government of India Tfr qd fuUra qanw darfiq Avlini stry o f A gri culture & F armers We lfare TR, FfrfrIfudr qii fuTrfi 6'-trflul frtmtTpspurl-ent of Agriculture, Cooperation& Farmers Welfare it;rFTfr riTqror, 'ilrtq ad'd?r6 frienilq DIRECTORATE OF PLANT PROTECTION, QUARANTINE & STORAGE (rd('E[ 4, intd6[rE (6kqtun )at.H.-rv, FAzuDABAD (HARyANA) - 121001 kianDatez2T/09/2018 To Director Agriculture Sector - 10, High Road, Krishi Bhavan, Gandhinagar. Gujarat,India. Sub: Advisory on current Status of Thrips (Thrips tabaci) for Cotton growing areas of Gujarat -reg. Sir, I have the honour to bring your kind notice that the incidence of Thrips on cotton crop was found at Low to Moderate level in Vadodara, Anand, Kheda, Bharuch, Narmada, Botad, Amreli, Surendra Nagar and Gandhrnagar districts of Gujarat. Keeping in view of the severity of the pest, it is advised that the all Cotton growing areas of Gujarat state may be intensively monitored during Rapid Roving Survey for assessment of population of Thrips. Therefore, strong linkage among State Agriculture Department, State Agricultural University, ICAR Institutes and farmers to implement Integrated Pest Management (IPM) at village level need to be developed. The following practices of IPM strategies may be followed for management of Thrips on Cotton crop 1. Grow attractarfiplants such as French bean to reduce Thrips infestation. 2. Conserve and augment natural enemy population such as Predatory mite (Amblyseius swirskii), predatory thrips (Aeolothrips sp. ),Insidious flower bugs (Orius insidiosus). 3. A strong and foolproof quality control system for fertilizers, bio-fertilizers, pesticides & bio pesticides needs to be enforced. A special campaign may be launched for quality control of fertilizers, bio -fertihzers, pe sticides & bio-pesticides. 4. Regular training programme for the extension workers, pesticide dealers and farmers should organizedby the SAUs/ICAR institutes/ClPMCs/ KVKs for up-gradation of their knowledge and skill regarding management of Thrips. 5. Insecticides must be used as per label claim approved by the Central Insecticides Board and Registration Committee detailed information is available at http:i/ppqs.gov.in/divisions/cib- rclmajor-uses-of-pesticides. However, list of recommended pesticides for Thrips is attached. (Annexure-I) IPM package of practices for Cotton need to be promoted. The IPM package of practise for Sugarcane may be downloaded from web-link In view of the above, it is advised to undertake monitoring of cotton crop on regular basis and if any more incidence of Thrips is reported by the farmers, extension functionaries and even through the newspapers or other source, survey of the affected area may be conducted immediately and the concemed officials at the Division/District/Block may be advised to take suitable plant protection measures immediately. The detailed status report may be sent to this Directorate through Fax (Nos. 0129-2412125 ot 0lI-23384182) or e- nrail: ppa@nic.in or appa.lpm-ppqs@eov.in urgently to apprise Department of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farmers Welfare. Yours faithfully, a ', ,{Nlfrl' fu.l.k.Snarma) Plant Protection Adviser Copy to: 1. Additional Secretary (PP), DAC&FW, MOA&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi. 2. Joint Secretary (PP&M&T), DAC&FW, MOA&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi' 3. Addl. Commissioner (Exten), Room No.",508,en,2018.0
