Advisory on incidence of Cassava mealy bug (Phenacoccus manihoti Matile-Ferrero) in Kerala.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on incidence of Cassava mealy bug (Phenacoccus manihoti Matile-Ferrero) in Kerala.pdf,0,")ffi{/rele : or2s- 2 4r3sss *ffilru x:0r29-24r2r2s E-mail: ppa@nic.in F. No. 3-6/2019-20flPM-AdvisorY ttT(f, {fGfiT of India TR q{ Rtff{ EF@TTUI Ti""Ffqn""Gvloinviesrtnrmy e o n f t A g iculture & Farmers welfare TR T{51ft:df qq futr1;[ EF'@TTUI fu[f{f /Department of Agricuuure, cooperation & Farmers Welfare TqHfr Ti(QTut, ffiq q{ {ff{ frtqffqql Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine And Storage gE {{.-4, S+ET{[E, ER9TU[/N.H.Iv. FARIDABAD (HARYANA) Date: o Q, June ,2020 To The Direclor of Agriculture Vikas Bhavan, Thiruvananthapuram Kerala 695033 Sub: Advisory on incidence of Cassava mealy bug (Phenacoccus manihoti Matile-Ferrero) in Kerala-regarding SirAvladam, I have the honogr to-bring to your kind notice that the incidence of Cassava mealy bug (phenacoccus manihoti Matile-Ferrero) has been confirmed and diagnosed/identified by the taxonomist at ICAR-NBAIR, Banga.lore based on diagnostic characteristics. As per the Pest alert issued by National Bureau of Agriculturally Important Insect Resources, NBAIR (copy enclosed), the pest was observed dn around 2000 square meter experimental plot of Cassava (Manihot esculenta Crantz) in Thrissur district of Kerala. As the pest is reported fol the first time in 'India, proactive interventions are imperative to manage and check its spread to new Af9as. Following strategies are suggested to contain, suppress and e#rlicate the pest population: To evade further spread of the pest, complete destruction by burning of the infested plants in the specific areas'is recommended. Farmers and other stake holders should be advised through extension functionaries to use suitable systemic chemical pesticides in heavily infested sites. Constant surveillance of the affected spot /kitchen gardens may be taken up involving stake holders. Awareness may be created in the affected village involving extension workers and public including women members of the family. :lh::;l:;;:::,:;:""r"";:1,:::,ffi 3;lt':h""Ii#:7""#',',::"",{i;,JJ'o!fi""5 which may support the carryover of the pest during absence of Cassava crop. Therefore, maintaining field sanitation and practicing clean cultivation is advised. Avoid use and transport of setts from the infested area for propagative purposes. In view of the Pest alert issued by NBAIR, it is advised to undertake monitoring of Cassava crop on regular basis. If any incidence of Cassava mealy bug is reported by the farmers, survey of the affected area may be conducted immediately and the concerned officials at district/division/block may be advised to take need based plant protection measures to contain/suppress/eradicate the pest population. The hot spots of Cassava mealy bug should be identified through survey for regular 'ap&ipm- monitoring. The detailed information may also be sent to the Directorate through e-mail ppqs@gov.in urgently to apprise the same to Department of Agriculture, Cooperation and Farmers Welfare. Yours faithfully Encl: As above Plant Protection Adviser Copy for information: 1. Joint Secretary(PP), DAC&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi-I10001 2. . PPS to PPA 3. Officer In-charge, CIPMC- Ernakulam with directions to conduct regular survey in the . area to ensure containment and eradication of the pest. al",467,en,2020.0
