Advisory on incidence of Citrus Psylla (Diaphorina citri) on Citrus in Amaravathi district of Maharashtra.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on incidence of Citrus Psylla (Diaphorina citri) on Citrus in Amaravathi district of Maharashtra.pdf,1,"""ttr-i""t1#-3""t#i,o?-a^frro-r, 0^*@*ou'tn urgentlv to apprise the same ro Department of Yours faithfully ,,&P/ Plant protection,{dviser Encl: as above Copy for information: j. i$sli?.Jf"" (pp), DA&FW, Kdshi Bhawan, NewDelhi-l10001. 3. Officer In-charge, RCIPMC. area 10 ensure contu'n-.n, -'r]ou eir-aTdrfcia t Y ro l n a h o a f : t a h s e h tpra e wi s th t . d irections to conduct regular survey in the",70,en,2022.0
Advisory on incidence of Fall Army Worm (FAW) on cotton crop in Maharashtra state.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on incidence of Fall Army Worm (FAW) on cotton crop in Maharashtra state.pdf,0,"\_-/ \_,/ ffi >dqtdTele : 0129 -Z 4t39gs ffT""*T*""M *us1p""*. 0129-2412125 @ E-mail: appa.ipm-ppqs@gov.in v.{ €./ No. 3 -6 /2019 -ZUlIpM_ Advisory +rn-,t gtqdG ovemment of India gR rt *sn qarur {*rcq/Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers werfare (5R' wr*rft-m gf F*'un uerror Fnrmy (Department of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farmers Welfare) *+wqfr frrersr, Tirrfrer cd {ierd frtvrra-q/Directorate of Plant Protection, euarantine & Storage qrga 4, wfrsrde (Efrqrun )/N.H._IV, Faridabad (Haryana) _ 121001 G:qislDate: 10th October. 20Ig To i. The commissioner of Agriculture, Commissionrate of Agriculture, Government of Maharashtra, Central Building, 3.d Floor, Pune-4 1 1001, Maharashtra. 2, The Director of Agriculture Extension & Training, -7 Commissionrate of A griculture 2""d Floor. Sahkar Sanful, Shivaji Nagar, pune-4 1 i 005, Maharashtra. 3. The Director of Agriculture Sector-10, High Road, Krishi Bhawan, Gandhinagar_3g20 1 0 Gujarat 4. The Commissioner and Director of Agriculture Old Mirchiyard, Nallapadu Road Chutru Guntam Guntur-522004 Andhra Pradesh. 5. The Commissioner Deparlment of Agriculture Government of Telengana Basheerbagh -500029 Hyderabad, Telengana 6. The Director of Agriculture Department of Agriculture Sheshadri Road, K.R., Circle Bangaluru-s6000 1, Karnataka 7. DirectorAgriculture Directorate of Agriculture Government of punjab KhetiBhawan Phase-6, Mohali Punjab- 160055 sub: Advisory on incidence of Falt Army worm (FAw) on cotton crop in Maharashtra state - regarding. 5lr. I have the honour to bring to your kind notice that as per the letter received from ICAR-Central Institute for { Cotton Research, Central Institute for Cotton Research (CICR), Nagpur, Maharashtra vide F.No. PS 1(FAWy2O19-20 dated 2Jtt'September, 2019 and,letter from cotton Improvement proiect. Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth, Rahuri vide Out No. Cotton/83312019 dated 20.09.2019, FAW has been reported for the first time in India on Cotton. This is the first record of FAW on Cotton in India invaded from infeste d. maize crop, so it is necessary to be alert about the infestation of FAW in Maharashtra and create awareness in the adjoining states: Gujarat, Andhra pradesh, Punjab, Karnataka and Telangana state. The following IPM Strategies should be followed for effective manasement of the pest. a Integratecl Pest management needs to be promoted by involving impor-tant pest management tools. a Monitoring and surveillance on regular basis and following IpM practices. a The inf-ested flowers and green bolls of cotton should be prornptly removed and destroyed. a Timely management at early instar level by hand collection of egg masses carrying leaves and destroying them with larvae. Trichog""amma parasitoids may be released directly or Tricho-card can be pinned to the leaves of standing cotton plants in the fields for destroying the egg stage. Use of neem based pesticide at initial stage of the pest for augmentation and conservation of potential parasitoids and predators. a Infested crop residues should be removed and destructed promptly. a Use glossy lure pheromone baited traps for the control of adult male moths. a Farmers must be advised to maintain field sanitation at the vicinity of the main field and nearby areas must be kept free liom weeds. Regular training programmes for the extension workers/ pesticide dealers and farmers should be organized for upgradation of knowledge and skill.",508,en,2019.0
Advisory on incidence of Fall Army Worm (FAW) on cotton crop in Maharashtra state.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on incidence of Fall Army Worm (FAW) on cotton crop in Maharashtra state.pdf,1,"a Farmers must be advised to maintain field sanitation at the vicinity of the main field and nearby areas must be kept free liom weeds. Regular training programmes for the extension workers/ pesticide dealers and farmers should be organized for upgradation of knowledge and skill. a Pesticides must be used as per label claim approved by the registration committee. a IPM package of practices for cotton need to be promoted the IPM package of practices for cotton can be downloaded from http://ppqs.gov.in/sites/default/flles/cotton.pdf or from http:llfarmers.gov.in. Regular meetings of State Pest Surveillance and advisory unit and District pest Surveillance and Advisory Unit may be conducted. As recommended from CICR, Nagpur, entomopathogenic fungi Metarhizium anisopliae @ 59 or Nomuraea rileyi @ 59 per litre of water may be sprayed on cotton crop. As recornmended from CICR, Nagpur, Spinetoram 1 1.7 SC @ 0.8 ml or Chlorantraniliprole l g.5 SC @ 0.3 ml per litre of water can be sprayed to already infested cotton crop to avoid further damage. Emamectin Benzoate 5% SG & 1'g%EC (approved pesticides for Pink Boll Worm (PBw) on Cotton) may also be used for the manasement of FAW in cotton. The hot spot of FAW should be identified for survey and teams may be constituted for regular surveillance and monitoring of FAW situation. Need based plant protection measures should be adopted to avoid economic loss to the cotton crop. Tirnely supply of qLralitv pesticides / bio-pesticides for the control of FAW on Cotton should be ensured. In view of the above, it is requested to monitor the cotton crop on regular basis and if major incidence of FAW is repofted by the iarmers, extension functionaries and even through newspapers or other sources, survey ofthe affected may be conducted immediately and the concerned officials at the district/ division/ block may be advised to take the suitable plant protection measures immediately. The detailed information may also be sent to the Directorate throueh email ppa@nic.in urgently to apprise the same to Depafiment of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farmers welfare. Yours faithfully -) rn""i""ffi Plant Protection Adviser Copy'to: 1. Additional Secretary(PP), MoA&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi-110001 2. Joint Secretary (PP), DAC&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi_l l000l J. PS to PPA 4. officer In-charges of CIPMCs Nagpur, Nashik, Bengaluru, Vadodara, Hyderabad, Jalandhar and Viiavawada. 400 | 1320 500-1000 Thrips l::sr 0,:.",387,en,2019.0
