e coming Rabi season, FAW may cause serious damage to Maize in the absence of regular rainfall. Therefore, it is requested to take all possible precautionary measures to minimize the effect of FAW during Rabi, 20t9-20 The following strategies are suggested to contain and suppress the FAW: .Follow deep ploughing before sowing!. This will expose FAW pupae to predators. rTimely and uniform sowing over a large area is advised. Avoid staggered sowing. rEncourage cultivation of maize hybrids with tight husk cover to reduce ear damage by FAW. oEnsure compulsory seed treatment with Cyantraniliprole 19 .8o/o + Thiamethoxam 19.\Yo FS @ 6 ml/kg of seed. This will provide effective protection against FAW for 15-20 days. rFollow intercropping of maize with suitable pulse crops. oErection ofbird perches @ lllacre during early stage ofthe crop (up to 30 days). .Sowing of 3-4 rorvs of trap crops (e.g. Napier) around maize field and spray with 5%oNSKE or Azadirachtin 1500 pprn as soon as the trap crop shows symptorn of FAW damage. oCollect and destroy egg mass and young larvae present in freld. .Application of dry sand in to the whorl of aflected maize plants soon after observation of FAW incidence in the field. .Application of Sand + lime in 9:1 ration in whorls in first thirty days of sowing. rlnstall pheromone traps in field @ lilacre to monitor and manage FAV/ . .Eggs parasitoids such as Trichogramma sp.",486,en,2019.0
Advisory on incidence of Fall Army Worm (FAW) Spodoptera frugiperda on Maize in Himachal Pradesh.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on incidence of Fall Army Worm (FAW) Spodoptera frugiperda on Maize in Himachal Pradesh.pdf,1,".Application of Sand + lime in 9:1 ration in whorls in first thirty days of sowing. rlnstall pheromone traps in field @ lilacre to monitor and manage FAV/ . .Eggs parasitoids such as Trichogramma sp. a'l,d Telemonus ren'rus can be released for destroying the egg stage of FAW (avoid spraying chemical pesticides for t-ew days during the time of release in the field). rEntomopathogenic fungi such as Metarhiziunt anisopliae, Nomuraea rileyi, Beauveria bassiana and Verticilium lecani may be extensively used for management of the pest. .The following chemical pesticides such as Spinetoram 11.7%SC or Chlorantraniliprole 18.5% SC or Thiamethoxam 12.6o/o+Lambda cyhalothrin 9.5%o ZC may be appiied up to early tasselling stage for controlling FAW. The chemical pesticides should be used on rotation basis. rThe fbcus rnay be given to suppress, contain and eradicate the pest at the earliest .lPM package of practices for Maize need to be promoted. The IPM package of practices can be down loaded llom http://ppqs. gov.in/ipm""packages. .Package of practices for management of FAW on maize need to be promoted. The IPM package of practices can be downloaded from http://ppqs.gov.in/advisories. rlnsecticides must be used as recommended by Central lnsecticide Board and Registration Committee (CIB&RC). Regular meetings of State Pest Surveillance & Advisory Unit (SPSAU) and District Pest Surveillance and Advisory units (DPSAU) may be conducted. The hot spots of FAW should be identified for survey and teams may be constituted for regular monitoring of FAW situation and adoption of need based plant protection measures to avoid economic loss. Timely supply of quality pesticides/ bio-pesticides for the control of FAW on Maize should be ensur:ed. In view of the above, it is requested to monitor the maize crop on regular basis and if major incidence of FAW is reported by the farmers, extension functionaries and even through newspapers or other sources,. survey of the aff-ected fields rray be conducted irnmediately and the concerned officials at the district/ division/ block may be advised to take the suitable plant protectiolr measures immediately. The detailed information may also be sent to the Directorate through email ppa@nic.in ureently to apprise the same to Department of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farrners Welfare. Yours faithfully r*"":.,.#Ict Piant Protection Adviser Copy to: 1. Additional Secretary(PP), MoA&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 2. Joint Secretary(PP), DAC&FV/, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 3. PS to PPA 4. Offtcer In-charges of RCIPMCs- Lucknow and Guwahati & CIPMCs- Patna, Aizwal, Imphal, Shillong, Dimapur, ltanagar, Agartala and Gangtok.",409,en,2019.0
