Advisory on incidence of Gundhi Bug (Leptocorisa acuta) on rice.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on incidence of Gundhi Bug (Leptocorisa acuta) on rice.pdf,1,"n :i"";i:{t** *f ililffi ';""1 $T# :: JT,TTI"" ii,,n. n .w e r i n g'!. iei: ^ffi m:11,;$ : stages;:ff;:: milkv se G riou * s diT f1 T # ; t ; o ;u r n ic o e i i o f ' p u r "" o g pe t/ r r m o a o n "" a e g a em . en h t e a s d tr s a r f e r g o v m n m ot il a k p v p l s ie ta d g ' e r h to e s E ra r l L n of this bug is s u""gJlidd?"". ""t -2- maturity. Therefore, it is requested to take all possible precautionary measures to minimize the eff'ect of Rice Gundhi blg (Leptocorisa acuta). The following strategies are suggested to contain and suppress the Rice Gundhi Bugs: o Strict vigilance is necessary at milky stage. o Keep the field and bunds free of weeds and grasses.. o Conservation of meadow grasshoppers, spiders, coccinellid beetles and dragonflies. o Putting attractants with an odor like dead snails or rats can easily capture rice bugs in the held. o Use of formulation of 10% sweet flag (Acorus calamus) rhizome powder and 90o/o of fly ash dust. . Use the following botanicals: Neem (Azadirachta indica) seed kernel extract 5o/o Notchi (Vitex negundo) leaf powdet extract 5o/o Pink morning glory (Ipomoea carnea) leaf powder extract 5Yo Prosopis (Prosopis cineraria) leaf powder extract 5Yo . Spray of 300m1 of formulation of Imidacloprid 06% + Lambda-cyhalothrin 04o/o SL in 500 liter water.Waiting period is l0 days. Insecticides must be used as recommended by CIB&RC. . IPM package of practices for rice need to be promoted. The IPM package of practices can be down loaded from http://ppqs.gov.inlipm-packages/eereals. The hot spots of Rice Gundhi Bug should be identified in pre-flowering spikelets stage and undertake need based plant protection measures to avoid economic loss. Timely supply of quality pesticides/ botanicals fbr the management of Rice Gundhi Bug on rice should be ensured. In view of the above, it is requested to monitor the rice crop on regular basis and if major incidence of Rice Gundhi Bug is reported by the farmers, extension functionaries and even through newspapers or other sources, survey of the affected fields may be conducted immediately and the concerned officials at the district/ division/ block may be advised to take the suitable plant protection measures immediately. The detailed information may also be sent to the Directorate through email ppa@nic.in urgently to apprise the same to Department of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farmers Welfare. Yours faithfully W (Dr.Ravi Praksh) Plant Protection Adviser Copy to: 1.PPS to Additional Secretary(PP), MoA&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 2.PPS to Joint Secretary(PP), DAC&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 3. PS tO PPA 4. Officer In-charges of RCIPMCs- Guwahati & Kolkata and CIPMCs- Aizwal, Imphal, Shillong, Dimapur, Gangtok, Agartala, Itanagar, Bhubaneswar, Patna, Ranchi fbr necessary follow-up.",503,en,
Advisory on incidence of Maize Stem borer (Chilo partellus) on maize crop in Uttar Pradesh.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on incidence of Maize Stem borer (Chilo partellus) on maize crop in Uttar Pradesh.pdf,0,"Phone:0129-2413985 E-rnail:-ppa@nic.in F.No 3-612022-23lIPM/Adviso rv $IT(Rfa{R/ Government of India ffr g4 frq""r{-d-.alnT ri?trcrq / Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Well'are TR, q{ ftfl? 6€qTor ft+ffi 7 pgp.6rn.nt of Agriculture & Farrners Wellare e-{eft{itQTur, {iiTterqd(iT{ft?sfldq / Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine & Storage qqq-q+, st'qTfl<(qfuraD - 121 001/NH-iv, Falidabad (l{a|vana) - 121 001 Dated: .08.2022 To The Director of Agriculture Directorate of Agriculture, Krishi Bhavan, Lucknow Uttar Pradesh- 226001 Sub: Advisory on incidence of Maize Stem borer (Chilo partellus) on maize in Farrukhabad district of Uttar Pradesh-reg. Sir, I have the honor to bring to youf kind notice that incidence of Maize Stem borer has been reported at Kamalganj block, Fan'ukhabad district of Uttar Pradesh as per the survey & reDolt on 22""d Julv 2022. The detailed surveillance carried out by RCIPMC Lucknow the level of infestation was found Low to Moderate (Above ETL) in 95 ha of maize crop. The larva feeds on the leaves by making a few ""shot holes"" and then boring downwards through the central whorl. It also cause internal tunnels by entering into the midribs and feeding on thi intemal tissues. The characteristic symptoms a|e ""shot holes"" during early stage and ,,dead heart,'during severe attack. Severe damage will result in breaking ofthe stem, and stunted gro*.th is reported. Larwae pupate inside the stern' Following strategies are suggested to contain, suppress and eradicate the pest population: * cotlect and destruct the stubbles & deep summer ploughing could kill hibernating PuPae .1. Install light traps @5lacre during night time to trap and kill the adults * Sowing of 3-4 rows of tr.ap crops (e.g. Napier) around maize field and spray with 5% NSKE or Azadirachtin 1500 ppm as soon as the trap crop shows symptom of stem borer damage * Inter-crop maize with cowpea in 2: I ratio .i. Erection ofbird perches @ l}lacre during early stage ofthe crop (up to 30 days) as birds acts as good predator on lepidopteran larvae To be continued in next Page ; -2- * Application of Sand + lime in 9: r ratio in whorls in first thirty days of sowing soon after the observation of stem borer incidence restricts larval feeding ' * f ' Two releases of rrichopyamma chironis g pards/ha (1,50,000 parasitized eggs/ha) conserve larval parasitoid cotesia flaiipes, pupal parasitoid retrastichus howardii, xanthopimla stemmator and preclators such as Chrysoperra carnea, spider, ear wig, coccinellid, dragor.r fly, preying mantid, pentatomid bug, reduviid bug, robber fly, rove bee es, wasp. * Granular application of carbofirran 3% cG @33.3kg/ha in whorls or infested plants or Dimethoate 30%EC @ 660 mIlha in 500- 1000 litre of water or Thiamerhoxam iz.ao y"" * Lambda-cyharothr in 09.50 6/o zc @ 125 ml/ha in 500 litre of water (waiting period is 42 days) to control stem borer. * Pesticide must be used as per label claim approval by the Registration committee. Detailed information is available at Directorate website. trttpyzpp'crs. sov. ;nraivisi;ns/ciu- rclmai or-uses-of-pesticides.",488,en,2022.0
