Advisory on Incidence of Papaya Mealybug ( Paracoccus marginatus) in Wardha district of Maharashtra.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on Incidence of Papaya Mealybug ( Paracoccus marginatus) in Wardha district of Maharashtra.pdf,0,"Phone: 0129-2476370 E-mail:-appa.ipm-PPqs@gov. in F.No 3-612019-20/IPl\OAdvisorv qT<iRfc|;T(/ Government of India 1ff1nifrerilfrcqruFiTtaq / Ministy of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare rm,q@Fr/DepartmentofAgicu1fure,Cooperation&FarmersWelfare iA-qfui<eTuf, Iir|tqqd(iq{frtqTqq / Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine & Storage qq\rq+, st-qEr<(aftqqD - 12l 001/ NH-IV, Faridabad (Haryana) - 121 001 Dated:as .07 .2022 To The Director of Hofticulture Opp. Netawadi, KB Joshi Path, Model Colony, Shivajinagar, Pune, Maharashtra 411005 Sub: Advisory on incidence of Papaya mealybug (Paracoccus maryinatus) on Papaya in Wardha district of Maharashtra -reg. Sir, I have the honor to bring to your kind notice that incidence ofPapaya mealybug have been reported at trace to moderale intensity in 4 acres of farmers field from Ghorad village, Selu Taluk, Wardha district of Maharashtra as per the survey report on 10'h -16'h June and 24s- 30'n June, 2022. Papayamealybuginfestationsaretypicallyobservedasclustersofcottonlikemassesonthe above-ground por.tion ofplants with long waxy filaments. Infestations on the stem results to stunting. deformationofnewgrowth,anddeathofthep|ant.ontheleavesthepestcausesyellowing' deformation, curling and early drop of leaves On the ftuits, there is a heavy build-up of honeydew and waxy secretions. The sooty mould develops due to the sugar in honeydew' which is the waste matter ofthe mealybugs. Fruits also become hard and very bitter to taste Following strategies are suggested to contain, suppress and eradicate the pest population: * To evade further spread of the pest, complete destruction by burning of the infested plants in the specific areas is recommended. * Awareness may be created in the affected village involving extension workers and public including rvomen members of the family * Constant sul""reillance of the affected spot ,&itchen gardens may be taken uP involving stake holders * The pest is found to survive and breed on weeds and crops |ike Hibiscus, Parthenium, Brinjal, Red gram, Jatropa, Bhindi, Custard apple, Guava elc which may support the carryover ofthe pest durirlgabsenceofPapayacrop.Therefore,maintainingfieldsanitationandcleancultivationis essential. * Application of sticky bands (or) alkathene sheet (or) a band of insecticide on arms (or) on main stem to prevent the movement of crawlers * prevention ofthe movement of ants and destruction ofalready existing colonies. In view ofthe Pest alert, it is advised to undertake monitoring of Papaya crop on regular basis. If any incidence of Papaya mealy bug is reported by the farrners, survey of the affected area may be conducted immediately and the concemed officials at district/division/block may be advised to take need based plant protection measures to cont4in/suppress/efudicate the pest popuiation. The hot spots of Papaya mealy bug should be identified tlrough survey for regular monitoring. The detailed information may also be sent to the Directorate through e-mail appaipm-ppqs@gov.in urgently to apprise the same to Depaftnent of Agriculture, Cooperation and Farmers Welfare. Yours faithfirlly ,,,-\*onP'>''v (Dr. J.P.Singh)l Plant Protection Adviser Encl: as above Copy for information: 1. Joint Secretary (PP), DA&F[ Kdshi Bhawan, New Delhi-110001. 2. PPS to PPA 3. Officer In-charge, RCIPMC- Napur, Maharashtra with directions to conduct regular suwey in the area to ensure containment and eradication of the oest. I :. li p",484,en,2022.0
