ow rust in the wheat growing areas Survey team has observed the incidence of Y€llow rust in trrce to high intensity in Nalvi khural, kunda kala, snd khiraipur villages of Karnal in traces in Jandhera village ofLaalwa (Kurukhetra) and Chhachhrauli block ofYamunanagar district. Yellow rust or Stripe rust is a disease ofwheat caused by a fungal pathogen' Prccinia .rr,'iilorr?n. The disease appears in the form ofyellow stripes on wheal leaves' This disease appears ifcoldtemperaturewithinlermittentrainscoincides'ThediseasemainLyappearsinthewheat groNing areas of Punjab, Haryana, Jammu and Kashmir an'l tarai regions ofUP and Uttrakhand' The first sign of stripe rust is the appearance of yellow streaks (pre-pustules)' followed by small, bright yelLow' and elongated uredial pustules arranged in consplcuous rows on rhe leave5, leafshealh.. glunet ar d a$n"" Inordertocontainthisdlseaseftombecominganepidemjcthefollowingpracticesof IPM stralegies may be followed for the managemenl ofYellow Rust in $heat crop: 1. Collect and destroy infested crop debris 2. Avoid ater logging in the field 3. Use lertilizers judiciously, fanners may be advised to avoid excess application of Nitrogen lertilizers. 4. Maintain field sanitalion 5. Farmers should be encouraged for adoplion olcultivation ofrust resistant varielies' 6. Regular training programme for the extension workers' pesticide dealers and farmers should be organized by the SAUS^CAR Institutes/CIPMCs/KVKs for up- gradalion oftheir knowledge and skill regarding identification of disease symptoms, anticipate environmental conditions conduclve for disease development and managemenl practices for yellow rust disease 7. Fungicides musl be used as per label claim approved by the Central lnsecticides Board and Regisiration Conmittee Detailed information is available al http://cibrc nic irlhup htm However' list ofrccommended fungicides for yellow rust is atlached herewith as (Annexure-l) 8.",504,en,2022.0
