 1) r a c o n sp. (larval) etc. Predators- Chrysotrterla carnea, Coccinellids, Reduviid bug, Pentatomid bug Trichograntma parasitoids may be released directly or Tricho-card can be pinned to the leaves of standing cotton plants in the fields lbr destroying the egg stage of PBW. . One spray of neem seed kemel extract (NSKE) 5Yo may be taken up at 60 days after sowing . Use of neem based pesticides (Annexure-I) in the initial stage of the pest for augmentation and conservation of potential parasitioids and pledators. r Use PB rope L Phermone traps (140 mg of a.i /dispensar & 9875 dispensars to be used for 25 ha of area) for the control of adult male moths. . Pesticides must be used as per label claim approved by the registration committee. Detailed information is available on directorate's website at lirk https://ppqs.sov.inlsites/default/files/1._maior use of oesticides insecticides as on 0 1.06.2023.pdf A list of recommended pesticides for pink boll worm is attached at Annexure-I. ............To b€ contd I -2- Further the following strategies should be adopted for spreading awaxeness among farmers Mobilization of extension functionaries at grass route level for regular monitoring of pest status. Regular meetings of State Pest Surveillance and advisory unit and District Pest Surveillaace e and Advisory Unit may be conducted f Awareness among farming commuity through newspapers, printing and electronic medi4 Kisan Gosthi, leaflet and pamphlets. I .",500,en,2023.0
