Advisory on management of Sesamia inferens (pink stem borer) in Wheat crop.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on management of Sesamia inferens (pink stem borer) in Wheat crop.pdf,0,"ffi & Phone: 0129-2413985 E-mail:-appa.ipm-ppqs@gov.in F.No 3-612022-23lIpM/Advisorv q|{iRr(6fv Government of India TR \ni frqrT F?TrrT ri?Taiq / Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers welfare 5& Ri ft{Ir{ fdqfq ArTIq / Department of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare q-i-qft *<HsI' rirrnq q* Tirr{Rt{I|uf{ l lir€ctorate of prant protection, euarantine & storage q{\rs4, 5ft{|{|{(Aftqrsn) _ l2l 001/ NH-IV, Faridabad (Haryan;) - 121 001 Dated: .02.2023 To The Director of Agriculture Punj ab Sub: Advisory on management oI Sesamia inferens (pink stem borer) in Wheat crop _reg. , Sir, This is to bring to your notice that the incidence of Sesamia inferens (pink stem borer) has repoted above moderate intensity from Wheat growing districts of Punjab state. It is a serious pest and may cause damage & eventually yield loss. Considering its status and host range which includes sugarcane, barley, oats, maize & fodder crops and keeping in view the current crop stage and prevailing weather conditions, population of this pest is expected to build up. Therefore, wheat crop should be monitored regularly for pest build up and adoption of Integrated pest Management techniques. Agro Ecosystem Analysis (AESA) based IpM package of practices of wheat are available at Dppe&s website in the link http://ppqs.gov.inlipm-packages. The Important IpM practices for management of Pink stem borer are listed belou: o Collection and destruction ofcrop debris. o Collect and destroy egq& larvae and infested parts ofplant. o Bird perches @ l0l acre should be erected for facilitating field visits ofpredatory birds. . Set up light traps @ 2 traps/ha for monitoring and mass trapprng lnsecrs. o Install Pheromone traps @5/ha. o Use ofpesticides should be need based and it should be used as per label claim approved by the Registration Committee. Detailed information is available on Directorate,s website in the link http://ppqs. goy. in/divi sions/cib-rc/maj or,uses-of_pgqlicides. Further the following strategies should be adopted for spreading awareness among farmers: Mobilization of extension functionaries at grass route level for regular monitoring of pests status. Awareness among farming community through newspapers, printing and electronic media, Kisan Gosthi, leaflet and pamphlets. The concerned officials at the district/ divisioni block level may be advised to take the suitable plant protection measures immediately Contd on page 2. 2 The detailed information- on pests' incidence may also be sent to the directorate through email lpa@qi:1l_ o_r appa'ipm-dpoos@gov.in urgently to apprise the same to Departnent of Agricurture & Farmers' Welfare. Your.s f aithfirlly Encl: as above r--) -ffip Plant Protection Adviser Copy for information: ' 2 I ' PPS to Joint Secretary (pp), DA & FW, Ikishi Bhawan, New Delhi- 1 1000 r The Director of Agricultur.e of other wheat growing states with the request to keep close ' 3. watch o p n p p A e st bu d up and take appropriate measures as mentioned above. PPS to for information. 4' officer-in-charges all cIPMCs of Wheat growing states with a direction to oonduct regular survey in their areas to ascertain the pest insidence level and neoessary foflow_up with the state authorities.",498,en,2023.0
