Advisory on South East Asian thrips (Thrips   parvispinus) on Chilli.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on South East Asian thrips (Thrips   parvispinus) on Chilli.pdf,0,"@ ffi Phone:0129-24'l63'70 E-mail:-appa.ipm- @ ppqs@gov.in q6 fE4 €d-dd-f €r 3rl{ F.No 3-612022-23lIPM-AdvisorY 3lT{d{RfrR/Govemment of India 1R""G B-Afa +""otot Fi?IFRI /Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare gR Vti B-Ora aAnw fra+rar7 Depanrneniof Agriculture, & Farmers Welfare Tm€cfr' d-{srrr, {i4nq a?i dJIo fr{rrr*q, rrd. (rq.4, FtErsK (6l{qrurD/ DIRECTORATE OF PLANT PROTECTION, QUARANTINE & STORAGE N.H.-IV, FARIDABAD (HARYANA) _ I21OO1 Dated: 15 .07.2022 lo, The Directors of Agriculture/ Hofticultue All States/ Union Territories Sub:-Advisory on South East Asian thrips (Thrips panispinus) on Chilli -reg. Sir, I have the honor to bring to your kind notice that hear,y infestation of South East Asian thrips (Thrips parvispirzz.rs) in chil1i crop occurred during Rabi 2021 in southem parts of the country leads to significant crop loss, there is possibility the pest may be expected to occur during the ongoing Kharif season based on availability of chilli crop and favourable weather conditions therefore monitoring of chilli crop is required well before devastating effect of invasive pest for adopting management measures at appropriate time and to avoid any economic loss to the farmers. The symptoms due to thrips damage include deep punctures and scratches on underside of the leaves leads to reddish decoloration and yellowing. Flower petals are also shows brownish streaks due to sucking of sap by thrips shows drying & withering and ultimately results in fruit loss. Booklet on ""Monitoring, Diagnosis and Management of South East Asian Thrips, Thrips parvispin zrs in Chilli"" was developed by DPPQ&S in consultation with ICAR incorporating biology of pest, identification key, damage symptoms, integrated management is strategies of pest which a ready reference for extention functionies and farmers for management of Invasive Chilli Thrips This booklet is available at the link http://ppqs.eov.in/sites/default/fi1es/south_east asian thrips thdos parvispinus- monitoring_and manasement.pdf The following IPM strategies are suggested in the booklet for the management of thrips on Chilli crop: o Raise seedlings in protrays under polyhouse condition with insect proof nets. Under open field conditions preference should be given for raised nursery beds and care should be taken to prevent the sucking pest infestation at nursery stage by monitoring the sucking pests with sticky traps o Collect and destroy infested crop debris. Uproot infected Chilli plants & weeds (Parthenium spp, Abutilon spp, Cleome viscosa, Prosopis sp., Lantana camara, Calotropis sp., Tecoma sp) present in the vicinity of field bunds which are acting as off season host to prevent further spread in freld. 113 Deep summer ploughing & frequent intercultural operaions (earthing up, raking of soil) to destroy pupae and residual stages ofthrips arrd other pests. Application of well decomposed farm yard manure (FYM) or compost @ 2'5 tlha, enriched with Metarhizium anisopliae or Pseudomonas fluorescens @ 2 kglt along with recommended doses of farm yard manure (25 to 30t/ha).",456,en,2022.0
Advisory on South East Asian thrips (Thrips   parvispinus) on Chilli.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on South East Asian thrips (Thrips   parvispinus) on Chilli.pdf,1,"Application of well decomposed farm yard manure (FYM) or compost @ 2'5 tlha, enriched with Metarhizium anisopliae or Pseudomonas fluorescens @ 2 kglt along with recommended doses of farm yard manure (25 to 30t/ha). Soil application of 500 kg of Neem cake and 1.50 -2.001 on of vermi-compost/ha to induce resistance against thriPs a Seed treatment with Imidachlorpid 70WS @10 g per kg seed' a Seedling root dip for 30 minutes with Imidachlorpid 17.8% SL @ 0'5 ml/ L' a Follow iecommended spacing (60 x 30 cm or 45 x 45 cm) and avoid close spacing, as the high density planting favors the pest incidence and multiplication' Balanced fertitization with enhanced potash application along with nitrogen and phosphorous fertilizers to induce plant resistance against the pest & avoid application of""*i""rr nitrogenous ferrili?ers as it makes plant prone to severe pest attack Border cropping with 2-3 rows of tall growing crops like sorghum I maize I bajta I fodder grasses etc. sown thickly as a barrier for thrips movement' Intercropping chilli with maize I sorghum and cowpea at 10:3:1 as barrier and 1. ""re*oii c.Jps for natural enemy multiplication, leading to biological control of thrips. Erection of blue or yellow/white sticky traps @ 65J5 traps/ha at crop canopy height for mass trapping purpose and 20-25 traps/ ha for monitoring purpose' Adopting sprinkler ir.rigation system instead of flood inigation, since the jet of water rp.uy fro- iprinklers disrupts the growth and multiplication ofthrips' Spraying of microbial based insectieid es like Beauveria bassiana or Lecanicilium tiroiii it4.00 g or m1/L (spore load - lx108 cfir/g or m1), Pseudomonas Jluorescence - NBAIRPFDWD at 20glL or Bacillus a/bas - NBAIR-BATP @ 20 g/L uniformly ' covering whole plant. . Foliar spray of Entomo Pathogenic Nematode (EPN), Steinernema carpocdpsae formulation atlOg/L + 1 gv/etting agent. soil application f EPNs, Steinernema carpocapsGe ot Heterorhabditis indica at1 .50- o tz.so kglha.It can be applied as soil drenching after mixing in 500 -750 L of water. EpN's are to be used early in the moming or during late evening hours as they are sensitive to uv and high temperature. spraying of EPNs in peak sunshine hours be avoided. Spraying o/o Neem Seed Kemel Extract (NSKE) or 57o Neem Seed Powder Extfact of O.SO% ft""""t"" oil (5 ml/L), 0.50% Pongamia oil (5 ml/L), and 5Vo Vitex negundo exffact (50 mli L) Spraying of commercial formulation of neem based insecticido (Azadilachtin3000 PPM) @2 ml,ll. (how much wateriha) Spraying of 2% Fish oil Rosin Soap (FoRS) (20 mlll) solely or in combination with Neem Seed Kemel Extract Spraying of sea weed (Kappapltycus alvarezii) exttact @ 2 ml/L fot inducing t""iirtutr."" in plant to withstand the severe incidence ofthrips.",446,en,2022.0
Advisory on South East Asian thrips (Thrips   parvispinus) on Chilli.pdf_002,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on South East Asian thrips (Thrips   parvispinus) on Chilli.pdf,2,"(how much wateriha) Spraying of 2% Fish oil Rosin Soap (FoRS) (20 mlll) solely or in combination with Neem Seed Kemel Extract Spraying of sea weed (Kappapltycus alvarezii) exttact @ 2 ml/L fot inducing t""iirtutr."" in plant to withstand the severe incidence ofthrips. The waiting periods mentioned against insecticide molecules (fumished in the annexure below) to be followed to avoid pesticide residues in the harvested produce' Repeated spraying of chemical insecticides with same mode ofaction and spraying of sub-lethal doses to be avoided to overcome thrips resurgence (sudden outbreak) Farmers are advised for spraying of registration committee approved label claim pesticides only which are attached as Annexure-I 2t3 Furtheritisadvisedthatchilligrowingareastobemonitoredonregularbasis andifanyincidenceofThripsisreportedbythefarmers'extensionfirnctionariesandeven through the newspapers or though any other so{rces, survey of the aflected area may be conductetl immediately and the concemed officials at the Division/Dishict/Block may be advised to take the suitable plant protection measures immediately. The detailed information may also be sent to this Directorate through e-mail ppa@nic.in or aopa.ipm-ppqs@gov'in urgently to apprise the same to the Departrnent of Agdculture & Farmers Welfme' Yours faithfi.rlly Encl: Annecxure-I (RC approved pesticides) Plant Protection Adviser Copy to: 1. PPS to Joint Secretary(PP), DAC & FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi- I 10001 2. PS to PPA f.Om""""rtn-ctturgesofClPMCsVijayawad4Hyderabad,Bengaluru'Ernakulum'Trichy& Nagpur for necessarY follow-uP )tJ I Annexure-I CIB-RC approved registered Pesticides for Thrips of Chilli Crop Common Dosage per ha Waiting name period from of a.i. (c) X'ormulation Dilution last the disease (glml\o water application to (t) harvest (in days) Acep