Advisory on White Grub (Holotrichia serrata) on Sugarcane crop.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Advisory on White Grub (Holotrichia serrata) on Sugarcane crop.pdf,0,"ffi ffi Phone:0129-2413985 E-mailippa@,nic.in F.No 3-6/2022-23fl PM/Advisorv fi{iRfCdfV Government of India 5R qE frqfd 6qrrr {""Terr / Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare dE f-* ftgn *qr""r FarFT / Department af Agriculture & Farmers Welfare qiqfr€a|fo,6nqqi{9€R?qTl(q/ Dircctorat€ of plant Protcction, Quarantine & storage \r{rs4, F€-{r{rE(Aftqrw) - 121 o0l/NHlv' Faridabad (Haryana) - 121 001 Datedr""i .o9.zo2z To The Directors of Agriculture Maharashtra Sub: Advisory on White Grub (Holotrichia sertala) on Sugarcane crop -reg' Sir, ThisistobringtoyournoticethattheincidenceofWhiteGrlb(Holotrichiaserrata)is reported above Economic Threshold Level (ETL) intensity from various parts of the sugarcane growing areas of Maharashtra state. white grub is an important soil pest of sugarcane which .C ma ' y cause serious damage in Sugarcane crop. Eggs of white grub are pear like white, grub is fleshy shaped whitish yellow in color. Pupae are tan to brown colored and found deeper in the soil while the adults are rusty red colored to black and i'eeds on the foliage of host trees like Neem, Ailanthus, Acacia etc. Therefore' sugarcane crop should be monitored regularly for pest build up and adopt Integrated Pest Management techniques.AgroBcosystemAnalysis(AESA)basedlPMPackageofpracticesofsugarcaneisavailable atDPPQ&Swebsiteinthelinkhttp://ppqs.gov.inlipm-packages.ImportantlPMpracticesforwhite grub are listed below: Management: o Provide adequate irrigation. r Collect and destroy the adult beetles harboring on Neem' acacia and other hosts' o Apply entopathogenic fitngus Beauveria brongniortii @ 2'5 kglha' r Entomopathogenic nematodes (EPNs) infected cadavers of Galleria/corcyra larvae containing live infective juveniles (us) are implanted in soil at plant bases at the rate of four cadavers per plant during May/ June and/or September for sugarcane root grub control' o Judicious use of Fipronil 40% + imidacloprid 40% WG@175-200 g in 400-500 litre of water/acre or phorate 10% CG @ 10,000 g/acre can be done ifpest attain ETL status' After harvesting: . Destroy the stubble in white grub infested fields properly . Avoid ratoon cropping . Deep ploughing immediately after harvesting .Stagnatingwaterupto24hrsinthefieldsothatthegrubwillcomeoutfromthesoil. Cont. on page 2 z i T ; h . e f d f e ii ta * ile '* d information on p u e r s g t e i n n t c ly id e t n o c e a p m p a .i y re a r a so . b * e r s "" e - n t t o to the directorate through email opa@nic.in Departrneft of Agricurture & Farmers, Encl: as above Yours faithfully (Dr. J.P. Sinsh) Plant Protection Adviier Copy for information: l. 2. lll R j^""*. """":""lar{(pp), DAc & FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi_ I 10001 ;fifl:fi':fff,til""Jffi::l^:*-"":-'.1s""**"" s""6'i*'*t"". 'with ppSto ppf iori""il;u;; annronnate measures as indicated above the requesr to keep crose +. officer In'charges' at cIpMCs ol^11*y: -'t survey in the area to ensurb and necessary follo g iv ro _ w u i p n G g t s fr h i t i e "" s , o w r i "" th a d u i t r h e o c r t i i t o ie n s s . to conduct regular",497,en,2022.0
