Current status of Late Blight (Phytophthora infestans) at Potato growing areas of Uttar Pradesh- Advisory.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Current status of Late Blight (Phytophthora infestans) at Potato growing areas of Uttar Pradesh- Advisory.pdf,0,"E-mail: ppa@nic.in afrstfr/T ere; 01292413985 thq{T/Tax : 0 l2g -241 2125 9=t €.iNo. 3 -6 12018^19/IPM-Advisory gT{A' TKiFKiGovernment of Ind i a Tfr qd fiF-q|;I ?F.qqIuI t'T|.F|-q /M in i stry of A gri cu ltLr re & Farrn ers We I fare TR, {rf,frIfudr qd fusrd f, rtrqlur fratrryp""ouftment of Agriculture, Cooperation& F-anners Welfare . a-tr€cfr TiTqilq', :d;r0rr qd tirA ftiqrmq DIT{ECTORATE, OF PLANT PROTECTION, QUARANTINE & STORAGII (rq(rq 4, st{rq-d (dfuqroTr )N. t{. - IV, FARIDA BA D ( FI ARy AN A) - I 2 1 0 0 I EaioDate: ol.ot.2ots To The Director of Agriculture Directorate of Agricultu re Government of Uttar Pradesh Lucknow *226001 Sub: Crrl rent status of Late Blight (Phytophthorn infestctns) at Potato gron,ing areas of Uttar Pradesh-Advisory reg. Sir, I wish to bring your kind notice that incidence of Late Blight (Phytophthora infestans) on Potato crop has been reported at Low to Moderate level in Agra, Mathura and Hathras districts of Uttar Pradesh state. Its infestation may further spread in other Potato growing areas of state if favourable weather conditions prevail. Keeping in view of the severity of the disease, it is advised that the all Potato growing areas of Uttar Pradesh state may be intensively monitored during Rapid Roving Survey for €ISSeSSrrIerr 'of infestation of Late blight. Therefore, strong linkage among State Agriculture Department, State Agricultural Universities, ICAR Institutions and farmers to implement Integrated Pest Management (IPM) at village level need to be developed. The following practices of IPM strategies may be followed for management of Late Blight disease in Potato crop 1. Collect and destroy infested crop debris. 2. Maintain field sanitation. 3. A strong and foolproof quality control system fbr fertilizers, bio-fcfiilizers, fungicides needs to be enr,,:ced. 4. Regular training programme for the extension workers, pesticide dealers and farmers should be organized by the SAUs/ICAR institutes/ClPMCs/ KVKs for up-gradation of their knowledge and skills regarding management of Late blight. 5. Fungicide must be used as per label claim approved by the Central Insecticides Board and Registration Committee, Detailed information is available at http ://ppq s. gov. inldivisions/cib- rclmajor-uses-of-pesticides However, list of recommended fungicides for Late Blight of (Annexure-I) Potato is attached. , 6. Farmers should be advised through extension functionaries to use only recommended doses of fertilizers and fungicides as per approved label claims by CIB&RC. 7. The IPM package of practices for Potato needs to be promoted. The IPM package of practices for Potato may be downloaded from web-link. http ://ppqs. gov. inlsites/default/fi les/potato.pdf In view of the above, it is advised to undertake monitoring of Potato crop on regular basis and if any more infestation of Late blight of Potato is reported by the farmers, extension functionaries and even through the newspapers or other sources, survey of the affected area may be conducted immediately and the concemed officials at the Division/District/Block may be advised to take suitable plant protection measures immediately. The detailed status report may be sent to this Directorate through Fax Q.{os.",497,en,
