"Current status of Rugose Spiraling Whitefly (RSW), Aleurodicus rugioperculutus Martin'on Coconut -Advisory.pdf_000",ppqs_advisories,"Current status of Rugose Spiraling Whitefly (RSW), Aleurodicus rugioperculutus Martin'on Coconut -Advisory.pdf",0,"E-mail: ppa@,nic.in tfffd/Tele : 01292 413 98 5 *-+Wnax: 01 29-2412125 ttrI TI./No . 3 -6 12018- 1 gilPM-Advis o ry flf{iT Stz5R/Government of India TR q.i F""gm qqlut dT|.tq /M i n i stry of Agri cu ltu re & Farnrers We I fare Tft, T(-fi""rkf,r qd'fiF.grd qqM hamynepartment of Agriculture, Cooperatiorr& Fanne rs We lfare ffi€qfr stqilur. TirRltr (r{:+16 heaTranr DIRECTORATII OF PLANT PROI'I1CTION, QUARANTINII & S'fORAGll (rd(rE 4, q-ttflqr{ Gft-qFryr )N.H.-tv, FARIDABAD (HARYANA) - l2l00 t Edi6/Dat"": To The Director Di recto rate of A gricultu re Govt. of Tamil Nadu Chennai-600005 Sub: Current status of Rugose Spiraling Whitefly (RSW), Aleurodicus rugioperculutus Martin'on Coconut -Advisory' reg. Sir, I wish to bring your kind notice that incidence of invasive and destructivc pcst, Rugose Spiralling ';Vhitefly (RSW), Aleurodicus rugioperculatus Martin on Coconut has been reported in above ETL (Economic Threshold Level) at Coimbatore, Ilrode and Tiruppur districts of Tamil Nadu. It's incidence may further spread to other Coconut growing areas if favourable weather conditions continue to prevail. Keeping in view of the severity of the pest, it is advised that all Coconut growing areas of Tamil Nadu state may be intensively monitored during Rapid Roving Survey for assessment of population of RSW. Therefiore, strong linkage among Statc Agriculture Department, State Agricultural University, ICAR Institutes and farmers to implement Intcgrated Pest Management (IPM) at village level need to be developed. The follo.' tng IPVI strategies may be adopted for manag,ement of Rugose Spiralling Whitefly (RSW) on Coconut: 1. Install yellow sticky traps in the orchards to trap adult whitcllics. 2. Encourage build up clf parasitoid(Encarsia sp. )in the orchards and re-introduce parasitized pupae in the whitefly infested orchards 3. Conserve and augment predators of RSW such as Crysoperla and, Coccinetticls which are available in the field. 4. Apply 7 oh starch stilution on leaflets to flakc out the sooty nroulds. 5. In severe cases, spray only neem oil 0.5% or NSKJi. 5V6 arcl avoid spraying any forrn of insecticides. 6. Itegular training programme for the extension workers and farmers should be organized by SAUs/ICAR institutes/ClPMCs/ KVKs for up-gradation of their knowledge and skill RSW regarding management of 7. Regular survey and surveillance should bee ccnonnrdrurccfteedd f fo o r r m onitoring thre incidence of Rsw. g. Sensitization and awareness programmes should be conducted to farmers and other stakeholders regarding IPM management strategies of RSW' g. Assessment of the population of RSW should be worked out and extent of damage should be determined to advice farmers accordingly for the effective management measures. In view of the above, it is advised that, the affected areas of Coimbatore, Erode and Tiruppur districts of Tamil Nadu should be monitored for RSW in coconut orchards on ,^.grrlu'. basis and if more incidence of Rugose Spiralling Whitefly is noticed by the farmers, extension functionaries ancl even througtt tft. newspapers or other source, survey of the affected area may be conducted immediately and the concerried officials at the DivisiorvDistrict/Block may be advised to take suitable plant protection measures immediately.",503,en,
"Current status of Rugose Spiraling Whitefly (RSW), Aleurodicus rugioperculutus Martin'on Coconut -Advisory.pdf_001",ppqs_advisories,"Current status of Rugose Spiraling Whitefly (RSW), Aleurodicus rugioperculutus Martin'on Coconut -Advisory.pdf",1,"basis and if more incidence of Rugose Spiralling Whitefly is noticed by the farmers, extension functionaries ancl even througtt tft. newspapers or other source, survey of the affected area may be conducted immediately and the concerried officials at the DivisiorvDistrict/Block may be advised to take suitable plant protection measures immediately. The detailed status report may be sent to thi ax (Nos' 0129-2412125 or 0ll-23384182) or e-mail: ppa@,nic.in or urgently to apprise Department of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farmers Welfare. Yours faithfully, /tt Raj (Sh. Plant Protection Adviser Copy to: 1. Joint Secretary (PP), DAC&FW, Krishi Bhawan. New Delhi. 2. Agriculture Commisstoner, Room No. 231, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi' 3. PS to PPA. 4. C)fficers I/C of ClpMCs-'frichy is instructedto keep close watch onthe population of RSW ancl be in touch with the State Agriculture Department for follow up action. 5. IT- Cell for uploading on DPPQ&S, website'",146,en,
Current status of Stem borer (Scirpophaga incertulas) at Rice growing areas of Uttar Pradesh.pdf_000,ppqs_advisories,Current status of Stem borer (Scirpophaga incertulas) at Rice growing areas of Uttar Pradesh.pdf,0,"E-mail: ppa@nic.in ffi efiqilarr etr""z or29z4t398s *ffi/tr'ax: 0129-2412125 tl=I Tf./I.{o. 3-6 |20l$-lgllPM-Advisory tlRd F{t5'R/Government of India tfr qii FiF-gta a?nsr derrq /\4inistry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare TR, Tf,firfufrIqEifugrfraanurRamrnepartment of Agriculture, Cooperation& Farmers Welfare irnrrF rkqrsr, drRfq qd drr6 fttqrwq DIRECTORATE OF PLANT PROTECTION, QUARANTINE & STORAGE (TdW 4, qIilqTE (6FqIgTI )A{.H.-[V, FARIDABAD (HARYANA) - 1 2 1 OO 1 *fo fuianDate:04110/2018 The Director Directorate of Agriculture Government of Uttar Pradesh Madan Mohan Malviya Marg Krishi Bhavan, Lucknow -226001 Sub: Current status of Stem borer (Scirpophuga incertulas) at Rice growing areas of Uttar Pradesh-Advisory reg. Sir, I have the honourlo bring your kind notice that incidence of stem borer (Scirpophaga incertulas) on rice crop has been reported at Low to Moderate level in Nari, Gauhari, Borka Bokhari, Jab chhoti, Bathan, Bari Bathan, Piparawala and Khadona villages and at Severe level in Gauhari, Nari and Semali villages of Chhata block of Mathura district of Uttar Pradesh state. Its incidence may finther spread in other rice growing areas of State if favourable weather conditions prevail. Keeping in view of the severity of the pest, it is advised that the all rice growing areas of Uttar Pradesh state may be intensively monitored during Rapid Roving Survey for assessment of population of Stem borer. Therefore, strong linkage among State Agriculture Department, State Agricultural University, ICAR Institutes and farmers to implement Integrated Pest Management (IPM) at village level need to be developed. The following practices of IPM strategies may be followed for management of Stem borer on rice crop 1. Farmers should be educated to identifu, conserve and augment the natural enemies available in the rice field viz., Parasitoids like Trichogramma spp., Tetrastichus schoenobii, Telenomus roruani, Amauromorpha accepta, Cotesia Jlavipes, Bracon sp., Xanthopimpla flavolineata, etc. and predators like Spiders etc. 2. Farmers should be advised through extension functionaries to use only recommended doses of fertilizers and pesticides as per approved label claims by GIB&RC. J a . A strong and foolproof quality control system for fertilizers, bio-fertilizers, pesticides & bio pesticides needs to be enforced. 4. Regular training programme for the extension workers, pesticide dealers and farmers should organized by the SAUs/ICAR institutes/ClPMCs/ KVKs for up-gradation of their knowledge and skill regarding management of Stem borer. 5. Insecticides must be used as per label claim approved by the Central Insecticides Board and RegistrationCommittee,Detailedinformationisavailableat rclmajor-uses-of-pesticides However, list of recommended pesticides for Stem borer is attached. (Annexure-I) 6, IPM package of practices for rice need to be promoted, The IPM package of practise for rice may be downloaded from web -link. http ://ppq s. eov. inlsite s/default/fi les/rice.odf In view of the above, it is advised to undertake monitoring of rice crop on regular basis and if any more incidence of Stem borer is reported by the far-.rs, extension functionaries and even through the newspapers or other iour.., in*.y of the affected area may be conducted immediately and the concemed officials at the Division/District/Block ma-y be advised to take suitable plant protection measures immediately. The detailed status report may be sent to this Directorati through Fax (Nos.",510,en,2018.0
