lanting and harvesting may be adopted zone wise. Detrashing the puparium bearing leaves and immediately disposing by burning or burying to prevent emergence of adult whiteflies. 5' Grow repellent plants such as Peppermint, at'rractarfi plants such as French bean and tall 6' border crops like Maize, Sorghum around the field to reduce whitefly infestations. Install yellow sticky traps to monitor the activity of whiteflies in field. 7.",477,en,2018.0
Current status of White Fly ( Aleurolobus barodensis ) at Sugarcane growing areas of Gujarat - Advisory.pdf_001,ppqs_advisories,Current status of White Fly ( Aleurolobus barodensis ) at Sugarcane growing areas of Gujarat - Advisory.pdf,1,"5' Grow repellent plants such as Peppermint, at'rractarfi plants such as French bean and tall 6' border crops like Maize, Sorghum around the field to reduce whitefly infestations. Install yellow sticky traps to monitor the activity of whiteflies in field. 7. Conserve and augment the natural enemies, Parasitoids such as Enacarsia spp, Eretmocerus spp., Dicyphus Hesperus, Chrysocharis spp (nymphal and pupal) and predators such as spiders, coccinellids, Lacewings, Mirid bug, Robber fly, Praying mantis, fire ants, Dragonfly and Big eyed bugs (Geocoris sp)' g. A strong and foolproof quality control system for fertilizers, bio-fertilizers, pesticides & bio pesticides needs to be enforced 9. Regular training programme for the extension workets, pesticide dealers and farmers should organizedby the SAUs/ICAR institutes/clPMCs/ KVKs for up-gradation of their knowledge and skill regarding management of White fly' 10. IPM package of practices for sugarcane need to be promoted. The IPM package of practise for Sugarcane may be downloaded from web-link- In view of the above, it is advised to rindertake monitoring of sugarcane crop on regular basis and if any more incidence of w;hite fly is reported by the farmers, extension * functionaries and even through the newspapers or other soufce, survey of the affected area may be conducted immediat-ely and the^concerned officials at the DivisiorVDistrict/Block -uy U. advised to take suitabll plant protection measures immediately. The detailed status report may be sent to this Directorate through Fax (Nos. 0129 -24t2t25 or 0ll-23384182) or e-mail: ppa@,nic.in o. appa.ipm-ppqs@,gorr. ""in urgently to apprise Departnient of Agriculture' Cooperation & Farmers Welfare. Yours faithfullY, t- ^uMrz (D.D.K.Sharma) Plant Protection Adviser Copy to: 1. Additional Secretary (PP), DAC&FW, MOA&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi' 2. Joint Secretarv GpgMA'f, OeC&FW, MOA&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi' a Addl. commissioner (Exten), Room No. 345, DAC&FW, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi' 4. Agriculture Commissiorr.r, fr.oo- No. 231, DAC&FW, MOA&FW,Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi. PPA. 5. PS to , officer I/C of cIpMC- Baroda is instructe&to keep watch on the incidence of Thrips 6. in cotton crop and be in touch with the state Govemment for follow up action' + +. T'.I Cr-\l {-t \^}ta""""t^^n Jlu voeb<''hc ' \\]",352,en,2018.0
