SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf_025,schemes,SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf,25,"Articles 1 Misc equipments such as auto titrators, bar code scanner & printer,etc - 51 51 ANNEXURE-VIII Illustrative list of Equipments for setting up of new State Govt Fertilizer Testing Labs S.No. Items No. 1 Inductively Coupled Plasma Spectrophotometer/ Atomic 1 Spectrophotometer (ICP/AAS) 2 Auto N-Analyzer 1 3 Spectrophotometer 1 4 Waster Bath-cum-shaker 1 5 Muffle Furnace + Oven 1 6 pH Meter 2 7 Vacuum Pump 2 8 Electronic Balance 2 9 Analytical Balance 1 10 Digestion/Distillation set 2 11 Karl Fisher Apparatus 2 12 Deionizer 1 13 Computer with appropriate software 1 14 Lab. Articles 1 Misc. equipments such as auto titrators etc - 52 52 Annexure-IX Illustrative list of equipment for Mini-lab S.No. Item Quantity 1. Balance 1 2. Shaker 1 3. Hot Plate 1 4. Meter to display readings 1 ________________________________ Added/Modified on 15.01.2016 53 53 54 Chapter 4 Continuation & Strengthening of Central Fertilizer Quality Control & Training Institute (CFQC&TI) 55 56 54 Continuation & strengthening of CFQC&TI 4.1 Analysis of Fertiliser Samples for Quality Control The CFQC&TI and its 03 Regional Laboratories are the notified labs under clause 29 of FCO for analysis of the fertilizer samples drawn by the fertilizer inspectors from fertilizer dealers and other sources. During 12th plan period it is proposed to continue analyse of fertilizer samples. 4.2 Human resource development through trainings directly by CFQC&TI and its 03 Regional Labs At CFQC&TI / RFCLs 4.2.1 Training Programme on Fertiliser Quality Control for Fertiliser Analyst- Four week duration with 20 participants in each course will be organized during 12th plan. 4.2.2 Training Programme on Fertiliser Quality Control for Fertiliser Inspectors - Two week duration with 20 participants in each course will be organized during 12th plan. 4.2.3 Training Programme on Fertiliser Quality Control for Fertiliser Enforcement officers of N.E. States Two week duration with 20 participants in each course will be organized during - 12th plan. 4.2.4 Training Programme on Fertiliser Quality Control for Notified authorities - One week duration with 20 participants in each course will be organized during 12th plan. 4.2.5 Training Programme on Fertiliser Quality Control for Foreign Participants - Five week duration with 20 participants in each course will be organized during 12th plan. In States 4.2.6 Training Programme on Fertiliser Quality Control for Fertiliser Enforcement/ Extension Officers - Two days duration with 50 participants in each course will be organized during 12th plan. 4.2.7 Training Programme on Fertiliser Quality Control for Fertiliser Dealers One days duration - with 50 participants in each course will be organized during 12th plan. 57 57 58 56 Chapter 5 Organic and INM Component of SHM 59 60 58 INM and Organic Component INM & Organic Component of SHM (Annexure-I) 5.1 Components to be implemented by NABARD are as under: 5.1.1 Setting up of mechanized Fruit/Vegetable Market/Agro Waste Compost production unit (3000 TPA capacity) 5.1.2 Setting up of State of art liquid/carrier based Bio-fertilizer/Biopesticide Production Units (200 TPA/50000 LPA Capacity) 5.2.",491,en,2016.0
SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf_026,schemes,SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf,26,"Components to be implemented by State Govts / ICAR / SAUs are as under: 5.2.1 Setting up of Biofertilizer and Organic Fertilizer Testing/Quality Control Laboratory (BOQCL) under FCO 5.2.2 Strengthening of existing Biofertilizer and Organic Fertilizer Testing/Quality Control Laboratory (BOQCL) under FCO 5.2.3 Support to research for development of organic package of practices specific to state and cropping system 5.2.4 Setting up of separate Organic Agriculture Research and Teaching Department 5.2.5 Promotion of Organic Inputs on farmer's field (Manure, Vermi-compost, Bio-Fertilizers Liquid / solid, Waste compost, Herbal extracts etc.) 5.2.6 Setting up of mechanized Fruit/Vegetable Market/Agro Waste Compost production unit (3000 TPA capacity) and Setting up of State of art liquid/carrier based Bio-fertilizer/Biopesticide Production Units (200 TPA/50000 LPA Capacity). 61 61 ANNEXURE –I Organic & INM Components of SHM Sl. Component Pattern of Assistance Remarks No 1 Setting up of Input Production Units and Soil Testing To be implemented by NABARD Labs in consultation with NCOF 1.1 Setting up of mechanized 33% of cost limited to Rs. For establishment of large Fruit/Vegetable market 63 lakh/unit for mechanized compost plants by waste/ Agro waste individuals/private agencies fertilizer companies / private compost production unit; through NABARD as industries / private entrepreneur / capital investment for 3000 individual etc. for fruit and vegetable TPA production capacity waste/agro waste compost unit Annexure-II 1.2 Setting up of State of art 25% of cost limited to Rs. For establishment of state of the art liquid/ carrier based 40 lakh/unit for individuals sterile liquid/carrier based Biofertilizer/ /private agencies through biofertilizers and microbial Biopesticide units; NABARD as capital biopesticides production units by investment of 200 TPA or fertilizer companies/ private 50000 LPA production industries/ private entrepreneur/ capacity individual etc Annexure III 1.3 Setting up of Soil Testing 33% of cost limited to For establishment of Soil Testing Laboratories Rs.25 lakh/lab for Labs (Static/ Mobile) with facility to (Static/Mobile) individuals / private analyse 12 parameters viz. pH, EC, agencies through OC, N, P, K, S, Zn, Fe, Mn, B & Cu NABARD as capital by fertilizer companies/ private investment per annum industries/ private entrepreneur/ analyzing capacity. individual etc. 1.4 Setting up of mini-lab 44% of cost limited to For establishment of mini-lab with developed by ICAR Rs.33000/ lab for facility to analyse 10 parameters viz. technology individuals/ private pH, EC, OC, N, P, K, S, Zn, Fe & B agencies through by fertilizer companies/ private NABARD as capital industries/ private entrepreneur/ investment for 3000 individual etc. samples per annum analyzing capacity 2 Setting up of Input Production Units State Governments shall send proposal for approval of Project Sanctioning Committee 2.1 Setting up of mechanized 100% Assistance to State For establishment of large Fruit/Vegetable market Govt/Govt. Agencies upto a mechanized compost plants by State waste/ Agro waste maximum limit of Rs. Government/APMCs/ compost production unit; Municipalities/other public sector 190.00 lakh /unit for 3000 enterprise etc. for fruit and vegetable TPA production capacity waste/agro waste compost unit under PPP or otherwise mode. 62 62 Sl.",494,en,2016.0
SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf_027,schemes,SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf,27,"Agencies upto a mechanized compost plants by State waste/ Agro waste maximum limit of Rs. Government/APMCs/ compost production unit; Municipalities/other public sector 190.00 lakh /unit for 3000 enterprise etc. for fruit and vegetable TPA production capacity waste/agro waste compost unit under PPP or otherwise mode. 62 62 Sl. Component Pattern of Assistance Remarks No 2.2 Setting up of State of art 100% Assistance to State For establishment of state of the art liquid/ carrier based Govt/Govt. Agencies upto a sterile liquid/carrier based Biofertilizer/ maximum limit of Rs. biofertilizers and microbial Biopesticide units; biopesticides production units by 160.00 lakh /unit for 200 State Government /APMCs/ TPA or 50000 LPA Municipalities/ other public sector production capacity enterprise etc. under PPP or otherwise mode. 3 Quality Control of Bio-fertilisers and Organic State Governments shall send Fertilisers proposal for approval of Project Sanctioning committee 3.1 Setting up of Bio - Assistance up to maximum For setting up of fertilizer and Organic limit of Rs. 85 lakh for new Biofertilizers/Organic Fertilizers fertilizer testing Quality laboratory Testing/Quality Control Laboratories Control Laboratory assistance as Grant -in-Aid shall be (BOQCL) provided to State Government Annexure IV 3.2 Strengthening of existing Assistance up to a For existing Biofertilizers/Organic Laboratory under FCO maximum limit of Rs. 45 Fertilizers Testi ng/Quality Control lakh for strengthening of Laboratories established by State existing infrastructure of Government under FCO assistance State Government shall be provided as Grant -in-Aid for Laboratory under their strengthening in terms of Agriculture or Horticulture equipments / instruments etc. Department. 4 State Governments shall send Promotion of Organic Input on Farmers’ Fields proposal for approval of Project Sanctioning committee 4.1 Promotion of Organic 50% of