cation (Annexure-I). 6.2 Expected Outcome The Scheme envisages: 6.2.1. Promotion of commercial organic production through certified organic farming. 6.2.2. The produce will be pesticide residue free and will contribute to improve the health of consumer. 6.2.3. It will raise farmer's income and create potential market for traders. 6.2.4. It will motivate the farmers for natural resource mobilization for input production. 71 71 ANNEXURE-I Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY) S.No Component Pattern of Assistance (in Rs) Remarks 1 Adoption of PGS certification through cluster approach State Governments shall propose to 1 2nd year 3rd year st year Project Sanctioning Committee an action plan for number of clusters for PGS certification 1.1 Mobilization of - - - For adoption of organic farmers / local people farming through cluster to form cluster in 50 approach under acre for PGS Participatory Guarantee certification System (PGS) certification, assistance will be provided for three year term. 1.1.1 Conducting of meetings 10000 0 0 State Government will and discussions of identify targeted 50 farmers in targeted acre area of cultivated areas to form organic fields of farmer for farming cluster @ Rs. formation of cluster.",504,en,2016.0
