SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf_032,schemes,SHM_Guidelines472016.pdf,32,"Data entry operator and consultant appointed at each cluster will be responsible for maintaining data 74 74 1.2.4 Soil sample collection 3990 3990 3990 LRPs will be responsible for and testing (21 collecting soil samples from both samples/year/cluster) agricultural and horticultural fields. @ Rs.190 per sample They will be tested by State/Central for three years soil testing laboratories / ICAR / SAUs laboratories. Based on the soil test results suitable package and practices o f organic farming will be recommended to members of a cluster. 1.2.5 Process 5000 5000 5000 The data entry operator and documentation of consultant will maintain both conversion into hard and soft copies of details of organic methods, packages and practices and PGS inputs used, certification process of individual cropping pattern farmer at office of followed, organic cluster. manures and fertilizer used etc., for PGS certification @ Rs.100 per member x 50 1.2.6 Inspection of fields 1200 1200 1200 LRPs of cluster will be of cluster member responsible for inspection of @ Rs. 400 each individual farmer’s field for /inspection x 3 (3 effective implementation of PGS inspections will be certification. The details of done per cluster observations on farming practices per year will be recorded and farmer diary will be maintained by LRPs. He will also guide each farmer about various practices of organic farming and also record it in diary. 1.2.7 Residue analysis 0 80000 80000 LRP members through of samples in association of NCOF/RCOF NABL (8 samples will per year per collect organic samples from cluster) @ Rs. selected field. The analysis of 10,000/ sample samples for pesticides and chemical residues will be don e by sending samples to NABL laboratories. 75 75 1.2.8 Certification Charges 0 2000 0 PGS certification will be given on the basis of inspection, documentation and sample testing. 1.2.9 Administrative 26150 16900 16900 Assistanc