SITAPUR.pdf_007,up_acp,SITAPUR.pdf,7,"Allow for grazing between 10AM to 3PM during cold i) Plantation of trees like Neem, Pipal, waves Allow the animals for Subabul around the shed grazing (normal timings) Feed green fodder/silage / concentrates during day time ii) Spreading of husk/straw/coconut leaves and roughages / hay during night time in case of heat on the roof of the shed waves iii) Water sprinklers / foggers in the animal Add 25-50 ml of edible oil in concentrates per kg and shed fed to the animal during cold waves iv) Application of white reflector paint on the roof to reduce thermal radiation Apply / sprinkle lime powder (5-10g per square feet) in effect the animal shed during cold waves to neutralize Cold wave : Covering all the wire meshed walls / ammonia accumulation open area with gunny bags/ polyethylene sheets Put on the foggers / sprinklers during heat weaves and with a mechanism for lifting during the day time heaters during cold waves in case of high productive and closing during night animals In severe cases, vitamin ‘C’ (5-10ml per litre) and electrolytes (Electral powder @ 20g per litre) should be added in water during severe heat waves. 18 2.5.2 Poultry Convergence/linkages with Suggested contingency measures ongoing programs, if any Before the event During the event After the event Heat wave Heat wave Shelter/environment Provision of proper In severe cases, foggers/water Routine practices Shelter/environment management shelter with good sprinklers/wetting of hanged gunny bags are followed management ventilation should be arranged Don’t allow for scavenging during mid day Health and disease Deworming and Supplementation of house hold grain Routine practices Health and disease management vaccination against RD Provide cool and clean drinking water are followed management and fowl pox with electrolytes and vit. C (5-10 ml per litre) In hot summer, add anti-stress probiotics in drinking water or feed (Reestobal etc., 10-20ml per litre) Cold wave